steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787475937
      nanos: 743872482
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Build a complete, polished, production-quality frontend for a modern AI product called **HALFTIME**.\n\nHALFTIME is an AI-powered hackathon command center that helps hackathon teams decide what to build, validate ideas, define an MVP, manage time, detect project risks, cut unnecessary features, manage limited AI resources, simulate judges, and prepare to ship.\n\nTAGLINE:\n\n**Stop. Recalculate. Ship.**\n\nThe product should feel like an intelligent teammate sitting beside a hackathon team during the final hours.\n\nThis is NOT a generic AI chatbot.\nThis is NOT a traditional admin dashboard.\nThis is NOT a simple collection of cards.\n\nThe frontend should feel like a premium startup product that could genuinely launch publicly.\n\n==================================================\n\n1. CORE UX PHILOSOPHY\n   ==================================================\n\nThe entire product should answer one question:\n\n**\"What should I do right now?\"**\n\nEvery important screen should communicate:\n\nCURRENT SITUATION\n\342\206\223\nWHAT IS WRONG\n\342\206\223\nWHAT HALFTIME RECOMMENDS\n\342\206\223\nWHAT THE USER SHOULD DO\n\342\206\223\nWHAT CHANGES AFTER THE ACTION\n\nThe interface should feel intelligent even before real AI is connected.\n\nUse realistic mock data.\n\nBuild the frontend so Gemini API and Supabase can be integrated later.\n\nDo NOT implement fake AI chat as the main experience.\n\nAI should appear through:\n\n* recommendations\n* warnings\n* scores\n* decisions\n* explanations\n* prioritization\n* next actions\n* judge feedback\n\n==================================================\n2. DESIGN DIRECTION\n===================\n\nCreate a distinctive visual identity combining:\n\n* premium AI workspace\n* developer productivity tool\n* hackathon mission control\n* modern editorial dashboard\n* futuristic but approachable SaaS\n\nReference the design quality of products such as:\n\nLinear\nRaycast\nVercel\nArc\nmodern AI workspaces\n\nDo NOT copy their layouts or branding.\n\nCreate an ORIGINAL HALFTIME identity.\n\nThe design should feel:\n\n* sophisticated\n* highly polished\n* intelligent\n* energetic\n* calm\n* slightly playful\n* premium\n* technical\n* memorable\n\n==================================================\n3. MORPHISM / VISUAL LANGUAGE\n=============================\n\nUse multiple modern UI techniques, but DO NOT apply every technique to every component.\n\nUse each visual technique intentionally.\n\n### GLASSMORPHISM\n\nUse selectively for:\n\n* AI recommendation panels\n* floating overlays\n* command palette\n* modal windows\n* resource insight panels\n* top-level floating controls\n\nUse:\n\n* translucent surfaces\n* background blur\n* subtle borders\n* layered transparency\n\nAvoid making the entire application glass.\n\n### SOFT NEUMORPHISM\n\nUse subtly for:\n\n* small controls\n* circular indicators\n* compact status controls\n* timer controls\n\nUse extremely subtle shadows.\n\nDo NOT make the UI look inflated or dated.\n\n### CLAYMORPHISM\n\nUse very lightly for:\n\n* featured AI recommendation\n* primary project health visualization\n* one or two hero elements\n\nSoft rounded depth is acceptable.\n\nDo not make every card look like clay.\n\n### AURORA / MESH GRADIENTS\n\nUse very subtle background gradients behind:\n\n* hero section\n* AI analysis state\n* Ship Mode\n* major transitions\n\nUse pastel colors rather than aggressive neon.\n\n### BENTO DESIGN\n\nUse a sophisticated bento-style information layout for the dashboard.\n\nDifferent information blocks should have different visual weights.\n\nDo NOT make every tile identical.\n\n### FLOATING SURFACES\n\nUse floating panels for:\n\n* Next Action\n* AI Recommendation\n* countdown\n* command actions\n\nCreate a layered sense of depth.\n\n### GLASS BORDER / HAIRLINE EFFECTS\n\nUse extremely thin translucent borders.\n\nCards should feel separated without looking boxed in.\n\n### SOFT GLOW\n\nUse subtle glow only for:\n\n* active navigation\n* AI status\n* primary CTA\n* critical countdown\n* successful scope cut\n* Ship Mode\n\nNever use glow everywhere.\n\n### GRADIENT TEXT\n\nUse very selectively for:\n\n* major hero heading\n* AI-related heading\n\nPrefer subtle pastel gradients.\n\n### MICRO-INTERACTIONS\n\nUse:\n\n* hover elevation\n* slight scale\n* soft fade\n* progress animation\n* button feedback\n* smooth transitions\n* number transitions\n* state transitions\n\nAnimations should feel expensive and polished, not flashy.\n\n==================================================\n4. COLOR SYSTEM\n===============\n\nDO NOT USE A WHITE BACKGROUND.\n\nDO NOT USE PURE BLACK.\n\nUse a deep colored foundation.\n\nBACKGROUND:\n\n#202B2A\n\nSURFACE:\n\n#293735\n\nELEVATED SURFACE:\n\n#31413F\n\nBORDER:\n\n#3B4B47\n\nPRIMARY ACTION:\n\nPastel Lime\n#C7F9A6\n\nAI:\n\nPastel Mint\n#A8E6CF\n\nINFORMATION:\n\nPastel Cyan\n#A8DADC\n\nWARNING:\n\nPastel Yellow\n#FFE0A3\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nPastel Coral\n#FFB7B2\n\nSUCCESS:\n\nPastel Green\n#B7E4C7\n\nPASTEL BLUE:\n\n#B8DDF0\n\nPASTEL VIOLET:\n\n#CDB4DB\n\nPRIMARY TEXT:\n\n#F0F4EE\n\nSECONDARY TEXT:\n\n#AAB8B2\n\nMUTED TEXT:\n\n#71817B\n\nUse pastel colors as semantic signals.\n\nLime = action\nMint = AI\nCyan = information\nYellow = warning\nCoral = critical\nGreen = healthy\nBlue = secondary information\nViolet = optional creative accent\n\nDo not make every component colorful.\n\n==================================================\n5. BRAND / LOGO\n===============\n\nUse a minimal geometric HALFTIME symbol.\n\nThe logo should subtly represent:\n\nHALF + TIME + MOMENTUM\n\nCreate an abstract H-like geometric mark with a deliberate interruption in the middle.\n\nThe interruption represents:\n\nPAUSE\n\342\206\222\nRECALCULATE\n\342\206\222\nMOVE\n\nUse a sophisticated pastel rainbow treatment across the symbol.\n\nUse:\n\nPastel Coral\nPastel Orange\nPastel Yellow\nPastel Lime\nPastel Mint\nPastel Cyan\nPastel Blue\nPastel Violet\nPastel Pink\n\nDo NOT create a literal rainbow.\n\nDo NOT create a clock.\n\nDo NOT create a stopwatch.\n\nThe logo should work as:\n\n* sidebar logo\n* favicon\n* app icon\n* loading indicator\n\nWordmark:\n\nHALFTIME\n\nUse a modern geometric font similar to Geist, Inter, or Satoshi.\n\n==================================================\n6. TYPOGRAPHY\n=============\n\nUse a premium modern sans-serif.\n\nRecommended:\n\nInter\nGeist\nSatoshi\n\nUse a monospaced font similar to:\n\nJetBrains Mono\n\nfor:\n\n* countdown\n* metrics\n* percentages\n* time estimates\n* technical information\n\nCreate strong hierarchy.\n\nLarge headings should be confident.\n\nSupporting text should be quiet.\n\nDo not use excessive font sizes.\n\n==================================================\n7. APPLICATION SHELL\n====================\n\nCreate a responsive application shell.\n\nLEFT SIDEBAR:\n\nLogo:\n\nHALFTIME\n\nSmall label:\n\nHACKATHON OS\n\nNavigation:\n\nOverview\nIdea Lab\nMVP Planner\nTasks\nResources\nJudge Mode\nLaunch\n\nUse clean line icons.\n\nActive navigation should have:\n\n* translucent surface\n* subtle pastel-lime glow\n* small indicator\n* smooth transition\n\nBottom:\n\nTeam DOOM\nSettings\n\nThe sidebar should collapse on tablet/mobile.\n\n==================================================\n8. TOP BAR\n==========\n\nDisplay:\n\nDORAHACKS 2.0\n\nTEAM DOOM\n\nOn the right:\n\n31 : 42 : 17\n\nTIME LEFT\n\nUse JetBrains Mono.\n\nCreate a subtle floating timer capsule.\n\nWhen time becomes critical, transition the timer visually toward pastel coral.\n\n==================================================\n9. MAIN DASHBOARD\n=================\n\nThis is the hero experience.\n\nA judge should understand the product in approximately five seconds.\n\nHero heading:\n\n**You\'re in the second half.**\n\nSubtitle:\n\n**Here\'s what matters right now.**\n\nBelow:\n\nPROJECT HEALTH\n\n72%\n\nAT RISK\n\nCreate a beautiful radial health visualization.\n\nUse layered rings and subtle depth.\n\nNext to it:\n\nTIME LEFT\n11h\n\nWORK LEFT\n14h\n\nCAPACITY GAP\n3h\n\n==================================================\n10. AI RECOMMENDATION\n=====================\n\nCreate a visually impressive floating glass/aurora panel.\n\nLabel:\n\nHALFTIME SAYS\n\nRecommendation:\n\n**\"You\'re 3 hours over capacity. Cut analytics and team profiles. Finish the core AI evaluation flow first.\"**\n\nShow a tiny animated AI indicator.\n\nButtons:\n\nRECALCULATE PLAN\n\nVIEW REASONING\n\nUse pastel mint/cyan accents.\n\nThe panel should look like HALFTIME has surfaced an important decision.\n\n==================================================\n11. NEXT ACTION\n===============\n\nCreate:\n\nYOUR NEXT MOVE\n\nFinish the core AI evaluation flow\n\nCRITICAL\n\n1h 20m\n\nReason:\n\n\"Everything else depends on this workflow.\"\n\nPrimary button:\n\nSTART TASK \342\206\222\n\nUse a floating surface with subtle depth.\n\nWhen clicked:\n\n* task becomes active\n* timer starts\n* dashboard state changes\n* toast appears\n\n==================================================\n12. PROJECT HEALTH BENTO\n========================\n\nCreate a sophisticated bento section.\n\nMVP\n82%\nON TRACK\n\nSCOPE\n64%\nTOO LARGE\n\nTEAM\n91%\nON TRACK\n\nRESOURCES\n48%\nLIMITED\n\nTESTING\n31%\nNEEDS ATTENTION\n\nDo not make all cards identical.\n\nUse different sizes and visual weights.\n\nUse thin animated progress indicators.\n\n==================================================\n13. TIME PRESSURE VISUALIZATION\n===============================\n\nCreate a beautiful visual comparison:\n\nTIME AVAILABLE\n11h\n\nWORK REQUIRED\n14h\n\nShow two elegant timeline bars approaching each other.\n\nHighlight:\n\n**3h OVER CAPACITY**\n\nUse pastel yellow/coral.\n\nThis should instantly communicate the core problem.\n\n==================================================\n14. SCOPE CUTTER\n================\n\nThis is one of the hero features.\n\nCreate:\n\n\342\234\202 CUT BEFORE YOU BUILD\n\nSubtitle:\n\nRecover time without hurting the demo.\n\nFeatures:\n\nAnalytics dashboard\n\342\210\2222h\n\nTeam profiles\n\342\210\2221h\n\nDark mode customization\n\342\210\22245m\n\nShow:\n\n3h 45m\n\nRECOVERABLE TIME\n\nButton:\n\nCUT SELECTED FEATURES\n\nWhen clicked, animate the transition:\n\nBEFORE:\n\n14h work\n11h available\n\360\237\224\264 AT RISK\n\nAFTER:\n\n10h 15m work\n11h available\n\360\237\237\242 ON TRACK\n\nUpdate:\n\n* project health\n* scope\n* work remaining\n* risk\n* dashboard recommendation\n\nShow:\n\n**3h 45m recovered. You\'re back on track.**\n\nThis interaction must be real.\n\n==================================================\n15. PROJECT SIGNAL\n==================\n\nProject:\n\nHackathon Copilot\n\nStatus:\n\nBUILD IT\n\nOverall:\n\n8.55 / 10\n\nShow:\n\nInnovation 8.7\nProblem Fit 9.2\nUsability 8.1\nExecution 8.4\nImpact 7.8\nFeasibility 9.1\n\nUse elegant horizontal visualizations.\n\n==================================================\n16. AI RESOURCE PRESSURE\n========================\n\nCreate:\n\nAI RESOURCE PRESSURE\n\nGemini\n78%\n\nBase44\n41%\n\nClaude\n84%\n\nUse floating progress bars.\n\nShow:\n\nHALFTIME SAYS\n\n\"Save Base44 credits for final polish.\"\n\nUse pastel mint/cyan.\n\nThese are manual demo values.\n\nDo NOT pretend to have real-time third-party credit access.\n\n==================================================\n17. ACTIVITY TIMELINE\n=====================\n\nCreate a minimal timeline.\n\nAI evaluation completed\n18m ago\n\nDashboard updated\n42m ago\n\nScope risk detected\n1h ago\n\nBuilder completed API\n1h ago\n\nUse small pastel status indicators.\n\n==================================================\n18. IDEA LAB\n============\n\nCreate a premium Idea Lab page.\n\nHeading:\n\nFIND SOMETHING WORTH BUILDING.\n\nInputs:\n\nTeam skills\nPersonal frustrations\nInterests\nTarget users\nAvailable time\nHackathon criteria\n\nButton:\n\nGENERATE IDEAS\n\nShow 3\342\200\2235 idea cards.\n\nEach card:\n\nIdea\nProblem\nTarget User\nInnovation\nProblem Fit\nFeasibility\nDemo Potential\n\nVerdict:\n\nBUILD\nMODIFY\nKILL\n\nUse beautiful hover interactions.\n\n==================================================\n19. MVP PLANNER\n===============\n\nSelected idea:\n\nHackathon Copilot\n\nShow:\n\nProblem\nTarget User\nSolution\nValue Proposition\n\nFeature sections:\n\nMUST BUILD\nSHOULD BUILD\nNICE TO HAVE\nCUT\n\nAllow features to move between groups.\n\n==================================================\n20. TASK BOARD\n==============\n\nCreate:\n\nBACKLOG\nTODO\nIN PROGRESS\nDONE\n\nTeam:\n\nBuilder\nDesigner\nGrowth\nProduct\n\nTask cards should show:\n\nTask\nOwner\nPriority\nEstimated time\n\nAllow drag-and-drop if supported.\n\n==================================================\n21. RESOURCES\n=============\n\nCreate:\n\nAI RESOURCE PRESSURE\n\nTool\nRemaining\nRecommended use\n\nGemini\n78%\nReasoning\n\nBase44\n41%\nFinal UI polish\n\nClaude\n84%\nCode review\n\n==================================================\n22. JUDGE MODE\n==============\n\nCreate an AI judge simulator.\n\nJudging criteria:\n\nInnovation \342\200\224 25%\nProblem Fit \342\200\224 20%\nUsability \342\200\224 20%\nExecution \342\200\224 15%\nImpact \342\200\224 10%\nFeasibility \342\200\224 10%\n\nShow:\n\n8.55 / 10\n\nThen prominently:\n\nWHY YOU MIGHT LOSE\n\n\"Your problem is strong, but your demo takes too long to reach the core value.\"\n\nThen:\n\nFIX BEFORE SUBMISSION\n\n1. Shorten onboarding\n2. Demo the core workflow first\n3. Remove unnecessary analytics\n\nThis page should feel brutally honest.\n\n==================================================\n23. LAUNCH MODE\n===============\n\nCreate:\n\nLAUNCH READINESS\n\n78%\n\nChecklist:\n\nMVP\nTesting\nCritical bugs\nDemo\nPitch\nREADME\nScreenshots\nDemo video\nProduct Hunt\nSocial launch\nSubmission\n\nStatuses:\n\nCOMPLETE\nNEEDS ATTENTION\nNOT STARTED\n\nCTA:\n\nENTER SHIP MODE \342\206\222\n\n==================================================\n24. SHIP MODE\n=============\n\nCreate a dramatic final state.\n\nUse an elegant dark surface with subtle aurora gradients.\n\nLarge heading:\n\n**You\'re not out of time.**\n\nSecond line:\n\n**You\'re out of unnecessary features.**\n\nButton:\n\nENTER SHIP MODE \342\206\222\n\nUse pastel lime.\n\nMake this feel like the culmination of the product.\n\n==================================================\n25. COMMAND PALETTE\n===================\n\nAdd a command palette accessible with:\n\n\342\214\230 K / Ctrl K\n\nCommands:\n\nGo to Dashboard\nFind Idea\nCreate Task\nCut Feature\nRun Judge\nCheck Resources\nEnter Ship Mode\n\nUse glassmorphism and backdrop blur.\n\n==================================================\n26. MICRO-INTERACTIONS\n======================\n\nUse high-quality micro-interactions:\n\n* hover elevation\n* subtle scale\n* button press\n* animated progress\n* smooth number changes\n* soft page transitions\n* sidebar transitions\n* toast notifications\n* skeleton loaders\n* AI thinking animation\n* status changes\n* feature removal animation\n* task completion animation\n\nDo NOT over-animate.\n\nEvery animation should communicate state.\n\n==================================================\n27. RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n=====================\n\nDesktop-first.\n\nAlso support:\n\nTablet\nMobile\n\nOn mobile:\n\n* collapse sidebar\n* use bottom navigation if appropriate\n* stack bento sections\n* preserve countdown\n* keep primary CTA accessible\n* avoid horizontal scrolling\n\n==================================================\n28. COMPONENT ARCHITECTURE\n==========================\n\nUse reusable components.\n\nExamples:\n\nAppShell\nSidebar\nTopBar\nCountdown\nHealthScore\nMetric\nAIRecommendation\nNextAction\nTimePressure\nScopeCutter\nIdeaCard\nTaskCard\nKanbanBoard\nResourceBar\nJudgeScore\nLaunchChecklist\nCommandPalette\nToast\n\nDo NOT put everything into one massive component.\n\nKeep components modular.\n\n==================================================\n29. DATA STRUCTURE\n==================\n\nUse realistic mock data.\n\nCreate clean types/interfaces for:\n\nTeam\nTeamMember\nHackathon\nProject\nIdea\nFeature\nTask\nResource\nJudgeEvaluation\nLaunchItem\n\nThe frontend should be structured so mock data can later be replaced with Supabase.\n\n==================================================\n30. AI-READY ARCHITECTURE\n=========================\n\nDo not connect Gemini in this initial frontend build.\n\nHowever, create clean placeholders for:\n\ngenerateIdeas()\nevaluateIdea()\ngenerateMVP()\nrecommendNextAction()\nrecommendScopeCuts()\njudgeProject()\n\nThese should currently return mock data.\n\nLater they will call Gemini server-side.\n\n==================================================\n31. QUALITY REQUIREMENTS\n========================\n\nThe result must feel like a real startup product.\n\nPrioritize:\n\n* visual hierarchy\n* spacing\n* typography\n* consistency\n* accessibility\n* responsiveness\n* interaction quality\n* loading states\n* empty states\n* error states\n* realistic data\n\nDo not make every component a card.\n\nUse visual hierarchy through:\n\n* typography\n* whitespace\n* bento layouts\n* floating surfaces\n* glass layers\n* subtle depth\n* gradients\n* borders\n* color signals\n\nUse morphism techniques intelligently rather than applying them everywhere.\n\n==================================================\n32. MOST IMPORTANT VISUAL RULE\n==============================\n\nThe product should look beautiful at first glance.\n\nBut beauty must never reduce usability.\n\nA user should immediately understand:\n\nTIME LEFT\n\342\206\223\nPROJECT HEALTH\n\342\206\223\nBIGGEST RISK\n\342\206\223\nNEXT ACTION\n\342\206\223\nWHAT TO CUT\n\nThe UI should make the team feel:\n\n**\"I finally know what I should do.\"**\n\n==================================================\n33. FINAL DEMO FLOW\n===================\n\nThe frontend should support this complete demo story:\n\nOpen Dashboard\n\n\342\206\223\n\nShow:\n\n11h remaining\n14h work\n\n\342\206\223\n\nHALFTIME identifies:\n\n3h capacity gap\n\n\342\206\223\n\nClick:\n\nRECALCULATE PLAN\n\n\342\206\223\n\nHALFTIME recommends:\n\nCut Analytics\nCut Profiles\nCut Dark Mode\n\n\342\206\223\n\nClick:\n\nCUT SELECTED\n\n\342\206\223\n\nDashboard updates:\n\n\360\237\237\242 BACK ON TRACK\n\n\342\206\223\n\nOpen Judge Mode\n\n\342\206\223\n\nShow:\n\n8.55 / 10\n\n\342\206\223\n\nShow:\n\nWHY YOU MIGHT LOSE\n\n\342\206\223\n\nFix the issue\n\n\342\206\223\n\nOpen Launch\n\n\342\206\223\n\nShow:\n\nLAUNCH READINESS\n\n\342\206\223\n\nENTER SHIP MODE\n\n\342\206\223\n\nFinal message:\n\n**You\'re not out of time.**\n**You\'re out of unnecessary features.**\n\n==================================================\nFINAL INSTRUCTION\n=================\n\nBuild the complete interactive frontend now.\n\nMake it visually exceptional, highly polished, responsive, modular, and startup-quality.\n\nUse morphism, bento layouts, subtle gradients, translucency, blur, depth, soft shadows, pastel accents, elegant animations, and modern interaction patterns where appropriate.\n\nDo NOT use all effects everywhere.\n\nThe goal is:\n\n**Maximum visual quality + maximum clarity + minimum visual clutter.**\n\nThe result should look like a product that could win a design-focused hackathon demo, not a generated template.\n\nBuild the frontend as a functional interactive application using mock data.\n\nDo not ask unnecessary questions.\nDo not wait for additional instructions.\nStart building.\n\n"
    items {
      text: "Build a complete, polished, production-quality frontend for a modern AI product called **HALFTIME**.\n\nHALFTIME is an AI-powered hackathon command center that helps hackathon teams decide what to build, validate ideas, define an MVP, manage time, detect project risks, cut unnecessary features, manage limited AI resources, simulate judges, and prepare to ship.\n\nTAGLINE:\n\n**Stop. Recalculate. Ship.**\n\nThe product should feel like an intelligent teammate sitting beside a hackathon team during the final hours.\n\nThis is NOT a generic AI chatbot.\nThis is NOT a traditional admin dashboard.\nThis is NOT a simple collection of cards.\n\nThe frontend should feel like a premium startup product that could genuinely launch publicly.\n\n==================================================\n\n1. CORE UX PHILOSOPHY\n   ==================================================\n\nThe entire product should answer one question:\n\n**\"What should I do right now?\"**\n\nEvery important screen should communicate:\n\nCURRENT SITUATION\n\342\206\223\nWHAT IS WRONG\n\342\206\223\nWHAT HALFTIME RECOMMENDS\n\342\206\223\nWHAT THE USER SHOULD DO\n\342\206\223\nWHAT CHANGES AFTER THE ACTION\n\nThe interface should feel intelligent even before real AI is connected.\n\nUse realistic mock data.\n\nBuild the frontend so Gemini API and Supabase can be integrated later.\n\nDo NOT implement fake AI chat as the main experience.\n\nAI should appear through:\n\n* recommendations\n* warnings\n* scores\n* decisions\n* explanations\n* prioritization\n* next actions\n* judge feedback\n\n==================================================\n2. DESIGN DIRECTION\n===================\n\nCreate a distinctive visual identity combining:\n\n* premium AI workspace\n* developer productivity tool\n* hackathon mission control\n* modern editorial dashboard\n* futuristic but approachable SaaS\n\nReference the design quality of products such as:\n\nLinear\nRaycast\nVercel\nArc\nmodern AI workspaces\n\nDo NOT copy their layouts or branding.\n\nCreate an ORIGINAL HALFTIME identity.\n\nThe design should feel:\n\n* sophisticated\n* highly polished\n* intelligent\n* energetic\n* calm\n* slightly playful\n* premium\n* technical\n* memorable\n\n==================================================\n3. MORPHISM / VISUAL LANGUAGE\n=============================\n\nUse multiple modern UI techniques, but DO NOT apply every technique to every component.\n\nUse each visual technique intentionally.\n\n### GLASSMORPHISM\n\nUse selectively for:\n\n* AI recommendation panels\n* floating overlays\n* command palette\n* modal windows\n* resource insight panels\n* top-level floating controls\n\nUse:\n\n* translucent surfaces\n* background blur\n* subtle borders\n* layered transparency\n\nAvoid making the entire application glass.\n\n### SOFT NEUMORPHISM\n\nUse subtly for:\n\n* small controls\n* circular indicators\n* compact status controls\n* timer controls\n\nUse extremely subtle shadows.\n\nDo NOT make the UI look inflated or dated.\n\n### CLAYMORPHISM\n\nUse very lightly for:\n\n* featured AI recommendation\n* primary project health visualization\n* one or two hero elements\n\nSoft rounded depth is acceptable.\n\nDo not make every card look like clay.\n\n### AURORA / MESH GRADIENTS\n\nUse very subtle background gradients behind:\n\n* hero section\n* AI analysis state\n* Ship Mode\n* major transitions\n\nUse pastel colors rather than aggressive neon.\n\n### BENTO DESIGN\n\nUse a sophisticated bento-style information layout for the dashboard.\n\nDifferent information blocks should have different visual weights.\n\nDo NOT make every tile identical.\n\n### FLOATING SURFACES\n\nUse floating panels for:\n\n* Next Action\n* AI Recommendation\n* countdown\n* command actions\n\nCreate a layered sense of depth.\n\n### GLASS BORDER / HAIRLINE EFFECTS\n\nUse extremely thin translucent borders.\n\nCards should feel separated without looking boxed in.\n\n### SOFT GLOW\n\nUse subtle glow only for:\n\n* active navigation\n* AI status\n* primary CTA\n* critical countdown\n* successful scope cut\n* Ship Mode\n\nNever use glow everywhere.\n\n### GRADIENT TEXT\n\nUse very selectively for:\n\n* major hero heading\n* AI-related heading\n\nPrefer subtle pastel gradients.\n\n### MICRO-INTERACTIONS\n\nUse:\n\n* hover elevation\n* slight scale\n* soft fade\n* progress animation\n* button feedback\n* smooth transitions\n* number transitions\n* state transitions\n\nAnimations should feel expensive and polished, not flashy.\n\n==================================================\n4. COLOR SYSTEM\n===============\n\nDO NOT USE A WHITE BACKGROUND.\n\nDO NOT USE PURE BLACK.\n\nUse a deep colored foundation.\n\nBACKGROUND:\n\n#202B2A\n\nSURFACE:\n\n#293735\n\nELEVATED SURFACE:\n\n#31413F\n\nBORDER:\n\n#3B4B47\n\nPRIMARY ACTION:\n\nPastel Lime\n#C7F9A6\n\nAI:\n\nPastel Mint\n#A8E6CF\n\nINFORMATION:\n\nPastel Cyan\n#A8DADC\n\nWARNING:\n\nPastel Yellow\n#FFE0A3\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nPastel Coral\n#FFB7B2\n\nSUCCESS:\n\nPastel Green\n#B7E4C7\n\nPASTEL BLUE:\n\n#B8DDF0\n\nPASTEL VIOLET:\n\n#CDB4DB\n\nPRIMARY TEXT:\n\n#F0F4EE\n\nSECONDARY TEXT:\n\n#AAB8B2\n\nMUTED TEXT:\n\n#71817B\n\nUse pastel colors as semantic signals.\n\nLime = action\nMint = AI\nCyan = information\nYellow = warning\nCoral = critical\nGreen = healthy\nBlue = secondary information\nViolet = optional creative accent\n\nDo not make every component colorful.\n\n==================================================\n5. BRAND / LOGO\n===============\n\nUse a minimal geometric HALFTIME symbol.\n\nThe logo should subtly represent:\n\nHALF + TIME + MOMENTUM\n\nCreate an abstract H-like geometric mark with a deliberate interruption in the middle.\n\nThe interruption represents:\n\nPAUSE\n\342\206\222\nRECALCULATE\n\342\206\222\nMOVE\n\nUse a sophisticated pastel rainbow treatment across the symbol.\n\nUse:\n\nPastel Coral\nPastel Orange\nPastel Yellow\nPastel Lime\nPastel Mint\nPastel Cyan\nPastel Blue\nPastel Violet\nPastel Pink\n\nDo NOT create a literal rainbow.\n\nDo NOT create a clock.\n\nDo NOT create a stopwatch.\n\nThe logo should work as:\n\n* sidebar logo\n* favicon\n* app icon\n* loading indicator\n\nWordmark:\n\nHALFTIME\n\nUse a modern geometric font similar to Geist, Inter, or Satoshi.\n\n==================================================\n6. TYPOGRAPHY\n=============\n\nUse a premium modern sans-serif.\n\nRecommended:\n\nInter\nGeist\nSatoshi\n\nUse a monospaced font similar to:\n\nJetBrains Mono\n\nfor:\n\n* countdown\n* metrics\n* percentages\n* time estimates\n* technical information\n\nCreate strong hierarchy.\n\nLarge headings should be confident.\n\nSupporting text should be quiet.\n\nDo not use excessive font sizes.\n\n==================================================\n7. APPLICATION SHELL\n====================\n\nCreate a responsive application shell.\n\nLEFT SIDEBAR:\n\nLogo:\n\nHALFTIME\n\nSmall label:\n\nHACKATHON OS\n\nNavigation:\n\nOverview\nIdea Lab\nMVP Planner\nTasks\nResources\nJudge Mode\nLaunch\n\nUse clean line icons.\n\nActive navigation should have:\n\n* translucent surface\n* subtle pastel-lime glow\n* small indicator\n* smooth transition\n\nBottom:\n\nTeam DOOM\nSettings\n\nThe sidebar should collapse on tablet/mobile.\n\n==================================================\n8. TOP BAR\n==========\n\nDisplay:\n\nDORAHACKS 2.0\n\nTEAM DOOM\n\nOn the right:\n\n31 : 42 : 17\n\nTIME LEFT\n\nUse JetBrains Mono.\n\nCreate a subtle floating timer capsule.\n\nWhen time becomes critical, transition the timer visually toward pastel coral.\n\n==================================================\n9. MAIN DASHBOARD\n=================\n\nThis is the hero experience.\n\nA judge should understand the product in approximately five seconds.\n\nHero heading:\n\n**You\'re in the second half.**\n\nSubtitle:\n\n**Here\'s what matters right now.**\n\nBelow:\n\nPROJECT HEALTH\n\n72%\n\nAT RISK\n\nCreate a beautiful radial health visualization.\n\nUse layered rings and subtle depth.\n\nNext to it:\n\nTIME LEFT\n11h\n\nWORK LEFT\n14h\n\nCAPACITY GAP\n3h\n\n==================================================\n10. AI RECOMMENDATION\n=====================\n\nCreate a visually impressive floating glass/aurora panel.\n\nLabel:\n\nHALFTIME SAYS\n\nRecommendation:\n\n**\"You\'re 3 hours over capacity. Cut analytics and team profiles. Finish the core AI evaluation flow first.\"**\n\nShow a tiny animated AI indicator.\n\nButtons:\n\nRECALCULATE PLAN\n\nVIEW REASONING\n\nUse pastel mint/cyan accents.\n\nThe panel should look like HALFTIME has surfaced an important decision.\n\n==================================================\n11. NEXT ACTION\n===============\n\nCreate:\n\nYOUR NEXT MOVE\n\nFinish the core AI evaluation flow\n\nCRITICAL\n\n1h 20m\n\nReason:\n\n\"Everything else depends on this workflow.\"\n\nPrimary button:\n\nSTART TASK \342\206\222\n\nUse a floating surface with subtle depth.\n\nWhen clicked:\n\n* task becomes active\n* timer starts\n* dashboard state changes\n* toast appears\n\n==================================================\n12. PROJECT HEALTH BENTO\n========================\n\nCreate a sophisticated bento section.\n\nMVP\n82%\nON TRACK\n\nSCOPE\n64%\nTOO LARGE\n\nTEAM\n91%\nON TRACK\n\nRESOURCES\n48%\nLIMITED\n\nTESTING\n31%\nNEEDS ATTENTION\n\nDo not make all cards identical.\n\nUse different sizes and visual weights.\n\nUse thin animated progress indicators.\n\n==================================================\n13. TIME PRESSURE VISUALIZATION\n===============================\n\nCreate a beautiful visual comparison:\n\nTIME AVAILABLE\n11h\n\nWORK REQUIRED\n14h\n\nShow two elegant timeline bars approaching each other.\n\nHighlight:\n\n**3h OVER CAPACITY**\n\nUse pastel yellow/coral.\n\nThis should instantly communicate the core problem.\n\n==================================================\n14. SCOPE CUTTER\n================\n\nThis is one of the hero features.\n\nCreate:\n\n\342\234\202 CUT BEFORE YOU BUILD\n\nSubtitle:\n\nRecover time without hurting the demo.\n\nFeatures:\n\nAnalytics dashboard\n\342\210\2222h\n\nTeam profiles\n\342\210\2221h\n\nDark mode customization\n\342\210\22245m\n\nShow:\n\n3h 45m\n\nRECOVERABLE TIME\n\nButton:\n\nCUT SELECTED FEATURES\n\nWhen clicked, animate the transition:\n\nBEFORE:\n\n14h work\n11h available\n\360\237\224\264 AT RISK\n\nAFTER:\n\n10h 15m work\n11h available\n\360\237\237\242 ON TRACK\n\nUpdate:\n\n* project health\n* scope\n* work remaining\n* risk\n* dashboard recommendation\n\nShow:\n\n**3h 45m recovered. You\'re back on track.**\n\nThis interaction must be real.\n\n==================================================\n15. PROJECT SIGNAL\n==================\n\nProject:\n\nHackathon Copilot\n\nStatus:\n\nBUILD IT\n\nOverall:\n\n8.55 / 10\n\nShow:\n\nInnovation 8.7\nProblem Fit 9.2\nUsability 8.1\nExecution 8.4\nImpact 7.8\nFeasibility 9.1\n\nUse elegant horizontal visualizations.\n\n==================================================\n16. AI RESOURCE PRESSURE\n========================\n\nCreate:\n\nAI RESOURCE PRESSURE\n\nGemini\n78%\n\nBase44\n41%\n\nClaude\n84%\n\nUse floating progress bars.\n\nShow:\n\nHALFTIME SAYS\n\n\"Save Base44 credits for final polish.\"\n\nUse pastel mint/cyan.\n\nThese are manual demo values.\n\nDo NOT pretend to have real-time third-party credit access.\n\n==================================================\n17. ACTIVITY TIMELINE\n=====================\n\nCreate a minimal timeline.\n\nAI evaluation completed\n18m ago\n\nDashboard updated\n42m ago\n\nScope risk detected\n1h ago\n\nBuilder completed API\n1h ago\n\nUse small pastel status indicators.\n\n==================================================\n18. IDEA LAB\n============\n\nCreate a premium Idea Lab page.\n\nHeading:\n\nFIND SOMETHING WORTH BUILDING.\n\nInputs:\n\nTeam skills\nPersonal frustrations\nInterests\nTarget users\nAvailable time\nHackathon criteria\n\nButton:\n\nGENERATE IDEAS\n\nShow 3\342\200\2235 idea cards.\n\nEach card:\n\nIdea\nProblem\nTarget User\nInnovation\nProblem Fit\nFeasibility\nDemo Potential\n\nVerdict:\n\nBUILD\nMODIFY\nKILL\n\nUse beautiful hover interactions.\n\n==================================================\n19. MVP PLANNER\n===============\n\nSelected idea:\n\nHackathon Copilot\n\nShow:\n\nProblem\nTarget User\nSolution\nValue Proposition\n\nFeature sections:\n\nMUST BUILD\nSHOULD BUILD\nNICE TO HAVE\nCUT\n\nAllow features to move between groups.\n\n==================================================\n20. TASK BOARD\n==============\n\nCreate:\n\nBACKLOG\nTODO\nIN PROGRESS\nDONE\n\nTeam:\n\nBuilder\nDesigner\nGrowth\nProduct\n\nTask cards should show:\n\nTask\nOwner\nPriority\nEstimated time\n\nAllow drag-and-drop if supported.\n\n==================================================\n21. RESOURCES\n=============\n\nCreate:\n\nAI RESOURCE PRESSURE\n\nTool\nRemaining\nRecommended use\n\nGemini\n78%\nReasoning\n\nBase44\n41%\nFinal UI polish\n\nClaude\n84%\nCode review\n\n==================================================\n22. JUDGE MODE\n==============\n\nCreate an AI judge simulator.\n\nJudging criteria:\n\nInnovation \342\200\224 25%\nProblem Fit \342\200\224 20%\nUsability \342\200\224 20%\nExecution \342\200\224 15%\nImpact \342\200\224 10%\nFeasibility \342\200\224 10%\n\nShow:\n\n8.55 / 10\n\nThen prominently:\n\nWHY YOU MIGHT LOSE\n\n\"Your problem is strong, but your demo takes too long to reach the core value.\"\n\nThen:\n\nFIX BEFORE SUBMISSION\n\n1. Shorten onboarding\n2. Demo the core workflow first\n3. Remove unnecessary analytics\n\nThis page should feel brutally honest.\n\n==================================================\n23. LAUNCH MODE\n===============\n\nCreate:\n\nLAUNCH READINESS\n\n78%\n\nChecklist:\n\nMVP\nTesting\nCritical bugs\nDemo\nPitch\nREADME\nScreenshots\nDemo video\nProduct Hunt\nSocial launch\nSubmission\n\nStatuses:\n\nCOMPLETE\nNEEDS ATTENTION\nNOT STARTED\n\nCTA:\n\nENTER SHIP MODE \342\206\222\n\n==================================================\n24. SHIP MODE\n=============\n\nCreate a dramatic final state.\n\nUse an elegant dark surface with subtle aurora gradients.\n\nLarge heading:\n\n**You\'re not out of time.**\n\nSecond line:\n\n**You\'re out of unnecessary features.**\n\nButton:\n\nENTER SHIP MODE \342\206\222\n\nUse pastel lime.\n\nMake this feel like the culmination of the product.\n\n==================================================\n25. COMMAND PALETTE\n===================\n\nAdd a command palette accessible with:\n\n\342\214\230 K / Ctrl K\n\nCommands:\n\nGo to Dashboard\nFind Idea\nCreate Task\nCut Feature\nRun Judge\nCheck Resources\nEnter Ship Mode\n\nUse glassmorphism and backdrop blur.\n\n==================================================\n26. MICRO-INTERACTIONS\n======================\n\nUse high-quality micro-interactions:\n\n* hover elevation\n* subtle scale\n* button press\n* animated progress\n* smooth number changes\n* soft page transitions\n* sidebar transitions\n* toast notifications\n* skeleton loaders\n* AI thinking animation\n* status changes\n* feature removal animation\n* task completion animation\n\nDo NOT over-animate.\n\nEvery animation should communicate state.\n\n==================================================\n27. RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n=====================\n\nDesktop-first.\n\nAlso support:\n\nTablet\nMobile\n\nOn mobile:\n\n* collapse sidebar\n* use bottom navigation if appropriate\n* stack bento sections\n* preserve countdown\n* keep primary CTA accessible\n* avoid horizontal scrolling\n\n==================================================\n28. COMPONENT ARCHITECTURE\n==========================\n\nUse reusable components.\n\nExamples:\n\nAppShell\nSidebar\nTopBar\nCountdown\nHealthScore\nMetric\nAIRecommendation\nNextAction\nTimePressure\nScopeCutter\nIdeaCard\nTaskCard\nKanbanBoard\nResourceBar\nJudgeScore\nLaunchChecklist\nCommandPalette\nToast\n\nDo NOT put everything into one massive component.\n\nKeep components modular.\n\n==================================================\n29. DATA STRUCTURE\n==================\n\nUse realistic mock data.\n\nCreate clean types/interfaces for:\n\nTeam\nTeamMember\nHackathon\nProject\nIdea\nFeature\nTask\nResource\nJudgeEvaluation\nLaunchItem\n\nThe frontend should be structured so mock data can later be replaced with Supabase.\n\n==================================================\n30. AI-READY ARCHITECTURE\n=========================\n\nDo not connect Gemini in this initial frontend build.\n\nHowever, create clean placeholders for:\n\ngenerateIdeas()\nevaluateIdea()\ngenerateMVP()\nrecommendNextAction()\nrecommendScopeCuts()\njudgeProject()\n\nThese should currently return mock data.\n\nLater they will call Gemini server-side.\n\n==================================================\n31. QUALITY REQUIREMENTS\n========================\n\nThe result must feel like a real startup product.\n\nPrioritize:\n\n* visual hierarchy\n* spacing\n* typography\n* consistency\n* accessibility\n* responsiveness\n* interaction quality\n* loading states\n* empty states\n* error states\n* realistic data\n\nDo not make every component a card.\n\nUse visual hierarchy through:\n\n* typography\n* whitespace\n* bento layouts\n* floating surfaces\n* glass layers\n* subtle depth\n* gradients\n* borders\n* color signals\n\nUse morphism techniques intelligently rather than applying them everywhere.\n\n==================================================\n32. MOST IMPORTANT VISUAL RULE\n==============================\n\nThe product should look beautiful at first glance.\n\nBut beauty must never reduce usability.\n\nA user should immediately understand:\n\nTIME LEFT\n\342\206\223\nPROJECT HEALTH\n\342\206\223\nBIGGEST RISK\n\342\206\223\nNEXT ACTION\n\342\206\223\nWHAT TO CUT\n\nThe UI should make the team feel:\n\n**\"I finally know what I should do.\"**\n\n==================================================\n33. FINAL DEMO FLOW\n===================\n\nThe frontend should support this complete demo story:\n\nOpen Dashboard\n\n\342\206\223\n\nShow:\n\n11h remaining\n14h work\n\n\342\206\223\n\nHALFTIME identifies:\n\n3h capacity gap\n\n\342\206\223\n\nClick:\n\nRECALCULATE PLAN\n\n\342\206\223\n\nHALFTIME recommends:\n\nCut Analytics\nCut Profiles\nCut Dark Mode\n\n\342\206\223\n\nClick:\n\nCUT SELECTED\n\n\342\206\223\n\nDashboard updates:\n\n\360\237\237\242 BACK ON TRACK\n\n\342\206\223\n\nOpen Judge Mode\n\n\342\206\223\n\nShow:\n\n8.55 / 10\n\n\342\206\223\n\nShow:\n\nWHY YOU MIGHT LOSE\n\n\342\206\223\n\nFix the issue\n\n\342\206\223\n\nOpen Launch\n\n\342\206\223\n\nShow:\n\nLAUNCH READINESS\n\n\342\206\223\n\nENTER SHIP MODE\n\n\342\206\223\n\nFinal message:\n\n**You\'re not out of time.**\n**You\'re out of unnecessary features.**\n\n==================================================\nFINAL INSTRUCTION\n=================\n\nBuild the complete interactive frontend now.\n\nMake it visually exceptional, highly polished, responsive, modular, and startup-quality.\n\nUse morphism, bento layouts, subtle gradients, translucency, blur, depth, soft shadows, pastel accents, elegant animations, and modern interaction patterns where appropriate.\n\nDo NOT use all effects everywhere.\n\nThe goal is:\n\n**Maximum visual quality + maximum clarity + minimum visual clutter.**\n\nThe result should look like a product that could win a design-focused hackathon demo, not a generated template.\n\nBuild the frontend as a functional interactive application using mock data.\n\nDo not ask unnecessary questions.\nDo not wait for additional instructions.\nStart building.\n\n"
    }
  }
}
