  planner_response {
    response: "I have designed and built the frontend for **HALFTIME** \342\200\224 the AI-powered hackathon command center (*\"Stop. Recalculate. Ship.\"*).\n\n### What Was Built\n\n- **Visual Identity & Theme**:\n  - Implemented the custom geometric **HALFTIME** brand mark featuring an interrupted bridge symbol representing the *Pause \342\206\222 Recalculate \342\206\222 Move* loop with subtle pastel rainbow accents.\n  - Deep-space canvas (`#202B2A`) paired with elevated surfaces (`#293735`, `#31413F`), hairline borders (`#3B4B47`), and semantic pastel color accents (Pastel Lime, Mint, Cyan, Yellow, Coral, and Green).\n  - Paired **Plus Jakarta Sans** and **Space Grotesk** display typography with **JetBrains Mono** for live countdowns, telemetry meters, and capacity estimates.\n\n- **Overview Dashboard & Live Midpoint Telemetry**:\n  - **Radial Health Visualizer**: Dynamic project health dial transitioning from `72% AT RISK` to `94% ON TRACK`.\n  - **Time Pressure Comparison**: Interactive timeline comparing 11h available runway against 14h of backlog work, highlighting the 3-hour capacity deficit.\n  - **HALFTIME Recommendation Surface**: Floating glassmorphic AI panel with live advice, automated recalculation, and a mathematical **Reasoning Trace** modal.\n  - **Next Move Card**: Direct execution trigger for *\"Finish the core AI evaluation flow\"* with live elapsed task timing.\n  - **Scope Cutter**: Hero interactive tool demonstrating the recovery of 3h 45m of runway by cutting non-essential modules (Analytics, Profiles, Themes) with real-time UI state updates and celebratory feedback.\n  - **Project Health Bento Grid & Activity Timeline**: Subsystem monitoring across MVP core, scope size, team status, resource limits, and dry-run rehearsals.\n\n- **Idea Lab**:\n  - Interactive idea synthesizer evaluating team skills, target users, and hackathon criteria into graded concepts with **BUILD**, **MODIFY**, or **KILL** verdicts and instant promotion to the MVP plan.\n\n- **MVP Planner**:\n  - 4-tier matrix (**MUST BUILD**, **SHOULD BUILD**, **NICE TO HAVE**, **CUT**) with fluid drag/click tier adjustments and dynamic hours calculation.\n\n- **Task Board & Sprint Execution**:\n  - Kanban board (**BACKLOG**, **TODO**, **IN PROGRESS**, **DONE**) with role-based filtering, task creation, and active task tracking.\n\n- **AI Resource Pressure**:\n  - Monitoring for Gemini 2.5 Flash (78%), Base44 UI Engine (41%), and Claude 3.7 Sonnet (84%) with credit burn alerts and optimization recommendations.\n\n- **AI Judge Simulator**:\n  - Calibrated against DoraHacks 2.0 weighted rubrics, surfacing *\"Why you might lose\"* feedback and actionable fixes that boost the score from 8.55 to 9.20.\n\n- **Launch Readiness & Ship Mode**:\n  - 11-gate launch readiness checklist and a dramatic **Ship Mode** culmination screen with celebratory particle effects and hackathon artifact verification.\n\n- **Command Palette (`\342\214\230K`) & Toast System**:\n  - Quick-action launcher for rapid navigation, scope trimming, and judge audits."
    thinking: "**Verifying First Steps**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the initial build and lint checks passed without a hitch. Now, I\'m meticulously revisiting the user\'s requirements, specifically the tagline and brand aspects. I\'m focusing on ensuring complete adherence to the demo flow.\n\n\n**Designing Visual Hierarchy**\n\nI\'ve been working on the visual architecture now. I\'ve chosen a deep-colored foundation for the UI, with specific pastel accents that are semantically linked to actions, AI, information, warnings, and critical issues. Glassmorphism and subtle aurora panels are strategically applied on decision surfaces. I\'m pleased with the color palette.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have designed and built the frontend for **HALFTIME** \342\200\224 the AI-powered hackathon command center (*\"Stop. Recalculate. Ship.\"*).\n\n### What Was Built\n\n- **Visual Identity & Theme**:\n  - Implemented the custom geometric **HALFTIME** brand mark featuring an interrupted bridge symbol representing the *Pause \342\206\222 Recalculate \342\206\222 Move* loop with subtle pastel rainbow accents.\n  - Deep-space canvas (`#202B2A`) paired with elevated surfaces (`#293735`, `#31413F`), hairline borders (`#3B4B47`), and semantic pastel color accents (Pastel Lime, Mint, Cyan, Yellow, Coral, and Green).\n  - Paired **Plus Jakarta Sans** and **Space Grotesk** display typography with **JetBrains Mono** for live countdowns, telemetry meters, and capacity estimates.\n\n- **Overview Dashboard & Live Midpoint Telemetry**:\n  - **Radial Health Visualizer**: Dynamic project health dial transitioning from `72% AT RISK` to `94% ON TRACK`.\n  - **Time Pressure Comparison**: Interactive timeline comparing 11h available runway against 14h of backlog work, highlighting the 3-hour capacity deficit.\n  - **HALFTIME Recommendation Surface**: Floating glassmorphic AI panel with live advice, automated recalculation, and a mathematical **Reasoning Trace** modal.\n  - **Next Move Card**: Direct execution trigger for *\"Finish the core AI evaluation flow\"* with live elapsed task timing.\n  - **Scope Cutter**: Hero interactive tool demonstrating the recovery of 3h 45m of runway by cutting non-essential modules (Analytics, Profiles, Themes) with real-time UI state updates and celebratory feedback.\n  - **Project Health Bento Grid & Activity Timeline**: Subsystem monitoring across MVP core, scope size, team status, resource limits, and dry-run rehearsals.\n\n- **Idea Lab**:\n  - Interactive idea synthesizer evaluating team skills, target users, and hackathon criteria into graded concepts with **BUILD**, **MODIFY**, or **KILL** verdicts and instant promotion to the MVP plan.\n\n- **MVP Planner**:\n  - 4-tier matrix (**MUST BUILD**, **SHOULD BUILD**, **NICE TO HAVE**, **CUT**) with fluid drag/click tier adjustments and dynamic hours calculation.\n\n- **Task Board & Sprint Execution**:\n  - Kanban board (**BACKLOG**, **TODO**, **IN PROGRESS**, **DONE**) with role-based filtering, task creation, and active task tracking.\n\n- **AI Resource Pressure**:\n  - Monitoring for Gemini 2.5 Flash (78%), Base44 UI Engine (41%), and Claude 3.7 Sonnet (84%) with credit burn alerts and optimization recommendations.\n\n- **AI Judge Simulator**:\n  - Calibrated against DoraHacks 2.0 weighted rubrics, surfacing *\"Why you might lose\"* feedback and actionable fixes that boost the score from 8.55 to 9.20.\n\n- **Launch Readiness & Ship Mode**:\n  - 11-gate launch readiness checklist and a dramatic **Ship Mode** culmination screen with celebratory particle effects and hackathon artifact verification.\n\n- **Command Palette (`\342\214\230K`) & Toast System**:\n  - Quick-action launcher for rapid navigation, scope trimming, and judge audits."
    thinking_duration {
