  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Design Choices**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the HTML details within the Artistic Flair template. Specifically, I\'m verifying the loaded fonts, comparing them against design guidelines to ensure consistency. The current setup includes Plus Jakarta Sans, JetBrains Mono, and Space Grotesk. My goal now is to integrate standard Inter and Plus Jakarta Sans variants to achieve a balanced typographical aesthetic.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Elements**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously examining several UI elements. The blur effect on the ambient background aura, achieved with a `div` element and specific CSS properties, provides a subtle, aesthetic touch. The floating AI online widget is working to ensure it\'s both functional and visually appealing. I\'m also breaking down the sidebar\'s brand logo box for potential modifications.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the aesthetic details of several components. I\'m taking a close look at the navbar active and inactive states. Specifically, I\'m considering the use of glow effects and shadow to reinforce active item visibility. I am also investigating font styles and gradient-based backgrounds within the navigation. I also just considered gradient to bottom right in the bottom team card. The goal is a clean, modern UI.\n\n\n**Evaluating Component Structures**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the specific code for the event header and associated components. I\'m focusing on the `Event` and `DORAHACKS 2.0` span elements, along with the \"Time Left\" and \"SHIP MODE\" capsules. My aim is to assess their structure and styling, including colors, fonts, and responsiveness within the provided framework.\n\n\n**Assessing Style Attributes**\n\nI\'m now deep in the details, meticulously reviewing the styling for two distinct cards. For the \"Project Health\" card, I\'m focusing on the `text-right` attributes and the visual nuances of the gauge component. I\'ve also been considering the \"Halftime Rec\" card, and the use of a badge to enhance its visual appeal. I\'m prioritizing consistency and clarity.\n\n\n\n**Reviewing Code Components**\n\nI\'m now zeroed in on a specific card structure, analyzing its components for optimization. The \"Intelligent Correction\" card includes a header, explanatory text, and action buttons. I\'m investigating the SVG background, and plan to review color choices, text hierarchy, and overall layout for improved readability and user engagement. I\'ll focus on how the action buttons and SVG interact with the rest of the layout, too.\n\n\n**Analyzing Component Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on a new component with several key features. I\'m assessing the core AI evaluation flow\'s structure, including visual elements like a crucial badge, and supporting elements such as the estimated time. I\'m also examining the scope cutter card, including the header, recoverable stats, and item selection flow. I\'m now exploring the overall UX of the task start buttons.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
