  user_input {
    user_response: "Continue working on the EXISTING HALFTIME application.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo NOT redesign the application.\nDo NOT change the existing color palette.\nDo NOT replace the existing layout.\nDo NOT rebuild the app from scratch.\nPreserve the current visual design exactly.\n\nThe goal of this step is to turn the dashboard from a visual prototype into a genuinely interactive product.\n\n==================================================\n\n1. WORKING COUNTDOWN\n   ==================================================\n\nMake the hackathon countdown functional.\n\nUse a configurable hackathon deadline.\n\nDisplay:\n\n31 : 42 : 17\nTIME LEFT\n\nThe countdown must decrease in real time.\n\nCreate a simple central configuration for:\n\nhackathonStart\nhackathonDeadline\n\nDo NOT use AI for countdown calculations.\n\nWhen time becomes low, change the visual status:\n\nNORMAL\n\342\206\222\nAT RISK\n\342\206\222\nCRITICAL\n\nUse the existing pastel warning/coral colors.\n\n==================================================\n2. PROJECT TIME ENGINE\n======================\n\nCreate deterministic project calculations.\n\nDemo values:\n\nTIME AVAILABLE:\n11 hours\n\nWORK REMAINING:\n14 hours\n\nCalculate:\n\ncapacityGap = workRemaining - timeAvailable\n\nCurrent state:\n\n3 hours over capacity\n\nShow:\n\n\360\237\224\264 AT RISK\n\nDo not ask Gemini to perform these calculations.\n\nUse normal TypeScript/JavaScript logic.\n\n==================================================\n3. YOUR NEXT MOVE\n=================\n\nMake the existing:\n\nYOUR NEXT MOVE\n\nsection functional.\n\nCurrent task:\n\nFinish the core AI evaluation flow\n\nEstimated:\n\n1h 20m\n\nWhen the user clicks:\n\nSTART TASK \342\206\222\n\nChange the task state to:\n\nIN PROGRESS\n\nShow:\n\nACTIVE\n1h 20m\n\nStart a small task timer.\n\nUpdate the Recent Activity section:\n\n\"AI evaluation task started \342\200\224 just now\"\n\n==================================================\n4. SCOPE CUTTER \342\200\224 CORE DEMO FEATURE\n===================================\n\nMake the Scope Cutter fully interactive.\n\nFeatures:\n\nAnalytics dashboard\nTime saved: 2h\n\nTeam profiles\nTime saved: 1h\n\nDark mode customization\nTime saved: 45m\n\nAllow the user to select/deselect each feature.\n\nShow dynamically:\n\nSELECTED:\n3 features\n\nRECOVERABLE:\n3h 45m\n\nThe button should say:\n\nCUT SELECTED FEATURES\n\nWhen clicked:\n\nRemove the selected features from the project\'s planned scope.\n\nUpdate:\n\nworkRemaining\ncapacityGap\nprojectHealth\nscopeScore\nriskStatus\nrecoverableTime\n\nBEFORE:\n\nWork remaining: 14h\nTime available: 11h\nCapacity gap: 3h\nStatus: \360\237\224\264 AT RISK\n\nAFTER CUTTING ALL THREE:\n\nWork remaining: 10h 15m\nTime available: 11h\nCapacity gap: -45m\nStatus: \360\237\237\242 ON TRACK\n\nShow a polished transition animation.\n\nShow a toast:\n\n\"3h 45m recovered. You\'re back on track.\"\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThis state must actually affect the dashboard.\n\nDo not simply animate numbers without changing the underlying state.\n\n==================================================\n5. PROJECT HEALTH\n=================\n\nMake Project Health respond to project changes.\n\nInitial:\n\n72%\nAT RISK\n\nAfter successful scope cutting:\n\nUpdate it to approximately:\n\n88%\nON TRACK\n\nThe exact calculation can be deterministic.\n\nUse a sensible simple formula.\n\nDo not use AI.\n\n==================================================\n6. TIME VS WORK VISUALIZATION\n=============================\n\nMake the existing Time Pressure visualization update automatically.\n\nBefore:\n\nTIME AVAILABLE\n11h\n\nWORK REQUIRED\n14h\n\n3h OVER CAPACITY\n\nAfter cutting:\n\nTIME AVAILABLE\n11h\n\nWORK REQUIRED\n10h 15m\n\n45m BUFFER\n\nChange the status from coral/amber to green/lime.\n\nAnimate the transition smoothly.\n\n==================================================\n7. PROJECT SIGNAL\n=================\n\nKeep the existing:\n\nHackathon Copilot\n8.55 / 10\n\nevaluation.\n\nFor now this remains mock data.\n\nDo not connect Gemini yet.\n\n==================================================\n8. RECENT ACTIVITY\n==================\n\nMake Recent Activity stateful.\n\nWhen actions occur, add new activity items.\n\nExamples:\n\n\"Scope reduced by 3h 45m \342\200\224 just now\"\n\n\"Project returned to ON TRACK \342\200\224 just now\"\n\n\"AI evaluation task started \342\200\224 2 min ago\"\n\nKeep the existing activity history.\n\n==================================================\n9. SIDEBAR NAVIGATION\n=====================\n\nMake every existing sidebar item functional:\n\nOverview\nIdea Lab\nMVP Planner\nTasks\nResources\nJudge Mode\nLaunch\n\nEach should navigate to the corresponding existing page.\n\nDo not create duplicate layouts.\n\nPreserve the existing design system across all pages.\n\n==================================================\n10. MOBILE\n==========\n\nCheck the existing application at mobile width.\n\nFix only genuine usability issues.\n\nEnsure:\n\n* no horizontal scrolling\n* sidebar collapses correctly\n* dashboard sections stack correctly\n* countdown remains visible\n* primary CTA remains accessible\n* Scope Cutter remains usable\n\nDo NOT redesign the desktop version.\n\n==================================================\n11. STATE ARCHITECTURE\n======================\n\nCreate a clean central project state.\n\nAt minimum track:\n\ntimeRemaining\nworkRemaining\nprojectHealth\nscopeScore\nriskStatus\nactiveTask\ntasks\nfeatures\nactivity\n\nUse reusable state/data structures.\n\nDo not duplicate the same project data in multiple components.\n\nKeep the architecture ready for Supabase later.\n\n==================================================\n12. QUALITY CHECK\n=================\n\nAfter implementing everything:\n\n1. Run/build the application.\n2. Check for errors.\n3. Check every navigation item.\n4. Test the countdown.\n5. Test START TASK.\n6. Test selecting features.\n7. Test CUT SELECTED FEATURES.\n8. Verify dashboard numbers update.\n9. Verify project status changes.\n10. Verify mobile layout.\n\nIf you find errors, fix them.\n\nDo not redesign working components.\n\nFINAL RULE:\n\nThe existing visual design is LOCKED.\n\nThis step is about:\n\n**FUNCTIONALITY, STATE, AND INTERACTION.**\n\nDo not start adding new features yet."
