    thinking: "**Analyzing Requirements Diligently**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the user\'s requirements, specifically a 12-point list. My current focus is designing a deterministic state engine to ensure all requested behaviors are precisely implemented. I am meticulously reviewing each point to build a clean and robust architecture. I\'ve begun checking the requirements point-by-point, with focus on making sure all functions correctly.\n\n\n**Implementing Countdown Functionality**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the countdown logic. I\'ve defined the display format and configured the central settings for start and end times. I\'m focusing on the visual status updates for different time thresholds, ensuring the use of pastel colors for alerts. The design is explicitly excluding AI, opting for a pure TS/JS approach with `setInterval`. Additionally, I\'ve started the time engine functions.\n\n\n**Evaluating Risk, Defining Next Steps**\n\nMy current analysis indicates a 3-hour capacity gap. I\'ve switched gears to the AI evaluation task, and I\'m initiating the core functionality to show its \'IN PROGRESS\' state. I\'ll need to integrate a live elapsed timer and update the recent activity section upon task start. I also started working on a \"Scope Cutter\" feature, which allows selecting features to cut from the project, providing a dynamic \"RECOVERABLE\" time based on selections. I will need to properly recalculate work remaining.\n\n\n**Calculating Project Health**\n\nI\'ve just finished the calculations based on the \"Scope Cutter\". The `timeAvailable` is 11h, but after scoping, the new time required is 10.25h. The calculation results in a capacity gap of -45m, representing a buffer. This positive change significantly boosts the `projectHealth` from 72% (AT RISK) to either 88% or even 94% (ON TRACK). The `scopeScore` jumps from 64% to an OPTIMAL 96%. This will trigger a system-wide update across the dashboard and give a toast message: \"3h 45m recovered. You\'re back on track.\"\n\n\n**Refining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI updates. I\'m focusing on the automatic time pressure visualization, ensuring a smooth animated transition reflecting the 45-minute buffer. I\'m maintaining the existing `Hackathon Copilot` evaluation data and building a dynamic activity timeline with real-time timestamps. Sidebar navigation remains fully functional, and I\'ve started checking mobile responsiveness, focusing on no horizontal scrolling and a clean, collapsible sidebar.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 904030955
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
