    thinking: "**Constructing the Countdown**\n\nI\'ve got the initial structure for the hackathon countdown implemented, targeting real-time updates. The core calculation is set up, directly using the provided deadline. I\'m focusing on the display format, striving for that 31 : 42 : 17 look. The goal is to avoid any reliance on AI for these countdown calculations, keeping it simple and efficient. The configuration aspects are now in development.\n\n\n**Refining the Status Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the visual status changes based on remaining time. The thresholds for \"NORMAL,\" \"AT RISK,\" and \"CRITICAL\" are set. I\'m leveraging those existing pastel colors and mapping them to these states. I am implementing configuration for event name, deadline, and total duration. I am using `secondsLeft` to define the baseline countdown logic. I\'ve designed the visual format and status badge for the top bar and status indicator.\n\n\n**Analyzing Capacity Changes**\n\nI\'ve just run a capacity check, and calculated I have a three-hour deficit. After the scope cut, I\'ll be in the green with a 45-minute buffer! I\'m now looking at the next section for an AI evaluation task, which should take one hour, twenty minutes. I\'ve noted down the button behavior and recent activity updates. The scope cutter also now looks good with dynamic toggles and recoverable time indicators.\n\n\n**Calculating Project Health**\n\nI\'ve just formulated a deterministic project health calculator! When work exceeds available time, it scales down from 80% to 50%; otherwise, health scales between 85% and 98%. I\'ve tested it with example scenarios, and I\'m updating the MVP Planner and Judge Mode to reflect the scope fix. Transitioning now to the overview dashboard\'s time and work visualization.\n\n\n"
