  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Requirements Architecturally**\n\nI\'m now diving into the architectural implications of those user needs, aiming for a clean implementation that respects the existing visual design constraints. I\'m focusing on the structural pieces needed and the interactions between them.\n\n\n**Designing Project Engine**\n\nI\'m architecting the `projectEngine` module. I am prioritizing the hackathon countdown, focusing on calculating remaining time and visual status (NORMAL, AT RISK, CRITICAL). I\'ve defined the data structures for timestamps and functions to format the countdown. Then I am designing the time and capacity engines, and defining how it calculates and tracks \"cut\" work items.\n\n\n**Calculating Project Health**\n\nI am now delving into the deterministic health and status calculations, considering `capacityGapMinutes`. The \'at-risk\' state triggers when the gap is positive, with a health score and scope score computed. Conversely, a negative gap indicates \'on-track\' status with different formulas. I\'m also including helper functions to format time in different formats, such as `formatHoursAndMinutes(minutes: number)` and `formatTimeLeft(seconds: number)`. The next step is processing the *Scope Cutter* feature, calculating recoverable time when the user selects and deselects features.\n\n\n**Implementing Scope Cutter Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing the scope cutter. When clicked, it will cut selected features, updating work remaining, capacity gap, and health metrics, while also displaying a toast and recent activity updates such as `\"Scope reduced by 3h 45m \342\200\224 just now\"` and `\"Project returned to ON TRACK \342\200\224 just now.\"` I\'m including a \"Restore scope\" option as well. I\'m focusing on the integration of state changes for tasks and visualizations. I\'ll animate the transition with visual progress bars. I\'ll maintain an updated project signal and recent activity section.\n\n\n"
