steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787477379
      nanos: 609586064
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Continue working on the EXISTING HALFTIME application.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n* Do NOT redesign the UI.\n* Do NOT change the current theme, colors, layout, logo, animations, or navigation.\n* Do NOT rebuild the application.\n* Do NOT remove existing functionality.\n* Preserve everything that currently works.\n\nThe goal of this step is to connect HALFTIME to the Gemini API safely and add real AI reasoning to the existing product.\n\n==================================================\n\n1. GEMINI ARCHITECTURE\n   ==================================================\n\nUse Gemini through a SERVER-SIDE API route.\n\nThe Gemini API key must NEVER be exposed in client-side code.\n\nUse an environment variable:\n\nGEMINI_API_KEY\n\nFrontend:\nUser action\n\342\206\223\nHALFTIME server/API route\n\342\206\223\nGemini\n\342\206\223\nStructured JSON\n\342\206\223\nFrontend\n\342\206\223\nUI update\n\nDo NOT call Gemini directly from browser/client code.\n\n==================================================\n2. CREATE ONE REUSABLE AI SERVICE\n=================================\n\nCreate a centralized Gemini service/module.\n\nCreate reusable functions:\n\ngenerateIdeas()\nevaluateIdea()\ngenerateMVP()\nrecommendNextAction()\nrecommendScopeCuts()\njudgeProject()\nimprovePitch()\n\nDo not duplicate Gemini API initialization throughout the application.\n\nKeep the AI layer modular so the Gemini model can be changed later.\n\n==================================================\n3. STRUCTURED OUTPUT\n====================\n\nDo NOT depend on free-form Gemini text.\n\nAsk Gemini to return structured JSON.\n\nFor example, an idea evaluation should return:\n\n{\n\"verdict\": \"BUILD\",\n\"overallScore\": 8.6,\n\"innovation\": 8.8,\n\"problemFit\": 9.2,\n\"usability\": 8.1,\n\"execution\": 8.5,\n\"impact\": 8.0,\n\"feasibility\": 9.0,\n\"strengths\": [],\n\"weaknesses\": [],\n\"recommendations\": []\n}\n\nValidate the response before sending it to the frontend.\n\nIf the response is invalid, gracefully show an error rather than breaking the application.\n\n==================================================\n4. IDEA LAB \342\200\224 REAL AI\n=====================\n\nConnect the existing Idea Lab to Gemini.\n\nInputs:\n\nTeam skills\nPersonal frustrations\nInterests\nTarget users\nAvailable time\nHackathon category\nJudging criteria\n\nWhen the user clicks:\n\nGENERATE IDEAS\n\nSend the information to Gemini.\n\nAsk Gemini to generate exactly 3\342\200\2235 ideas.\n\nEach idea must contain:\n\nname\nproblem\ntargetUser\nsolution\ninnovationScore\nproblemFitScore\nfeasibilityScore\ndemoPotential\nverdict\n\nThe AI must NOT generate generic ideas.\n\nTell Gemini to prioritize:\n\n* real problems\n* clear users\n* hackathon feasibility\n* strong demo potential\n* originality\n* narrow MVP scope\n\nDisplay the results using the EXISTING Idea Card design.\n\nAdd loading state:\n\n\"HALFTIME IS THINKING...\"\n\nDo not create a chat interface.\n\n==================================================\n5. IDEA KILLER / IDEA EVALUATION\n================================\n\nConnect idea evaluation to Gemini.\n\nWhen a user selects an idea, send:\n\nidea\nproblem\ntarget user\nsolution\navailable time\nteam skills\nhackathon judging criteria\n\nAsk Gemini to critically evaluate it.\n\nImportant:\n\nGemini should NOT blindly praise the idea.\n\nIt must be allowed to return:\n\nBUILD\nMODIFY\nKILL\n\nExample:\n\nKILL:\n\n\"This solves a crowded problem without enough differentiation.\"\n\nMODIFY:\n\n\"Strong problem, but the target user is too broad.\"\n\nBUILD:\n\n\"Clear pain point, achievable MVP, and strong demo potential.\"\n\nDisplay:\n\nOverall score\nInnovation\nProblem Fit\nUsability\nExecution\nImpact\nFeasibility\n\nUse the existing visual components.\n\n==================================================\n6. MVP PLANNER \342\200\224 REAL AI\n========================\n\nWhen the user selects an idea and clicks:\n\nGENERATE MVP\n\nSend the selected idea and constraints to Gemini.\n\nReturn:\n\nproblemStatement\ntargetUser\ncoreSolution\nvalueProposition\n\nfeatures:\n\nmustBuild[]\nshouldBuild[]\nniceToHave[]\ncut[]\n\nAlso return estimated build time.\n\nThe most important instruction:\n\nThe MVP must be achievable within the user\'s remaining hackathon time.\n\nDo not generate huge feature lists.\n\nThe AI should aggressively control scope.\n\nDisplay the result in the existing MVP Planner.\n\n==================================================\n7. NEXT ACTION RECOMMENDATION\n=============================\n\nConnect the dashboard\'s:\n\nHALFTIME SAYS\n\nto Gemini.\n\nGive Gemini the current project state:\n\ntime remaining\nwork remaining\ntasks\nteam members\ncurrent project\nfeatures\nproject health\nrisk status\n\nAsk:\n\n\"What is the single most valuable thing this team should do next?\"\n\nReturn:\n\nnextAction\npriority\nestimatedTime\nreason\nrisk\nalternativeAction\n\nExample:\n\n{\n\"nextAction\": \"Finish the core AI evaluation flow\",\n\"priority\": \"CRITICAL\",\n\"estimatedTime\": \"1h 20m\",\n\"reason\": \"Everything else depends on this workflow.\"\n}\n\nDisplay this inside the EXISTING AI recommendation component.\n\nDo not redesign it.\n\n==================================================\n8. SCOPE CUTTER \342\200\224 AI RECOMMENDATIONS\n====================================\n\nKeep the existing deterministic Scope Cutter.\n\nThe existing application already knows:\n\nfeature\nestimatedTime\ndependencies\npriority\n\nNow add Gemini reasoning.\n\nSend Gemini:\n\nproject\nfeatures\nremainingTime\nremainingWork\njudgingCriteria\n\nAsk Gemini:\n\n\"Which features should this team cut first while preserving the project\'s core value and judging potential?\"\n\nGemini should return:\n\nfeature\nreason\ntimeSaved\nimpact\nrecommendation\n\nExample:\n\nAnalytics:\nCUT\n\nReason:\n\"Consumes 2 hours but does not improve the core demo.\"\n\nTeam profiles:\nCUT\n\nReason:\n\"Not required for the primary user journey.\"\n\nDark mode customization:\nCUT\n\nReason:\n\"Visual polish is less valuable than completing the core workflow.\"\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nGemini recommends.\n\nThe application\'s normal logic performs the actual time calculations.\n\nDo NOT allow Gemini to directly modify project state.\n\n==================================================\n9. JUDGE MODE \342\200\224 REAL AI\n=======================\n\nConnect Judge Mode to Gemini.\n\nUse these exact judging weights:\n\nInnovation & originality \342\200\224 25%\nProblem-solution fit \342\200\224 20%\nUsability & design \342\200\224 20%\nExecution & craft \342\200\224 15%\nImpact & storytelling \342\200\224 10%\nFeasibility & scale \342\200\224 10%\n\nAsk Gemini to act as a skeptical hackathon judge.\n\nInput:\n\nproblem\ntargetUser\nsolution\nfeatures\ntechnical implementation\ndemo flow\nimpact\n\nReturn:\n\ninnovation\nproblemFit\nusability\nexecution\nimpact\nfeasibility\noverallScore\nbiggestWeakness\nwhyYouMightLose\nimprovements[]\n\nDo not make the judge overly positive.\n\nThe most useful feedback should be specific and uncomfortable.\n\nDisplay:\n\nWHY YOU MIGHT LOSE\n\nThen:\n\nFIX BEFORE SUBMISSION\n\nUse the existing Judge Mode design.\n\n==================================================\n10. PITCH COACH\n===============\n\nIf Pitch Coach already exists, connect it to Gemini.\n\nGenerate:\n\nProblem\nWhy it matters\nSolution\nHow it works\nDemo moment\nImpact\nWhy now\n\nAlso generate a concise 60\342\200\22390 second pitch.\n\nKeep the output structured.\n\n==================================================\n11. AI ERROR HANDLING\n=====================\n\nThis is essential for public launch.\n\nHandle:\n\nAPI failure\ntimeout\nrate limit\ninvalid JSON\nempty response\nnetwork error\n\nNever show:\n\n500 Internal Server Error\n\nInstead show:\n\n\"HALFTIME AI is temporarily unavailable.\"\n\nThen:\n\n\"Your project data is safe. Try again in a moment.\"\n\nThe dashboard, timer, tasks, Scope Cutter calculations and saved project state must continue working without Gemini.\n\n==================================================\n12. LOADING STATES\n==================\n\nUse the existing visual language.\n\nDuring AI generation:\n\nHALFTIME IS THINKING...\n\nUse a subtle animation.\n\nFor idea generation:\n\nAnalyzing team strengths...\nFinding real problems...\nTesting feasibility...\nPreparing recommendations...\n\nDo not use fake long delays.\n\nKeep the loading experience short and professional.\n\n==================================================\n13. RATE LIMIT PROTECTION\n=========================\n\nProtect the Gemini endpoint.\n\nDo not allow unlimited anonymous requests.\n\nCreate a simple server-side rate limit.\n\nFor the MVP, use a reasonable per-user/IP request limit.\n\nIf the limit is reached, show:\n\n\"You\'ve reached the current AI usage limit. Try again later.\"\n\nDo not expose API details.\n\n==================================================\n14. SECURITY\n============\n\nNever expose:\n\nGEMINI_API_KEY\n\nto:\n\nwindow\nlocalStorage\nclient JavaScript\npublic environment variables\n\nOnly use it server-side.\n\nDo not log the API key.\n\nDo not send secrets to Gemini.\n\n==================================================\n15. MOCK FALLBACK\n=================\n\nCreate a fallback mock response for development/testing.\n\nIf Gemini is unavailable in development, the UI can use mock AI responses.\n\nClearly structure this so production can disable the mock fallback if desired.\n\n==================================================\n16. DO NOT CHANGE EXISTING UI\n=============================\n\nThis is critical.\n\nKeep:\n\n* current colors\n* current typography\n* current logo\n* current layout\n* current sidebar\n* current animations\n* current dashboard\n* current Scope Cutter\n* current navigation\n\nOnly connect real AI behind the existing interface.\n\n==================================================\n17. TEST THE FULL FLOW\n======================\n\nAfter implementation, test:\n\nIDEA LAB\n\342\206\223\nGenerate ideas\n\342\206\223\nSelect idea\n\342\206\223\nEvaluate idea\n\342\206\223\nGenerate MVP\n\342\206\223\nCreate features\n\342\206\223\nDashboard\n\342\206\223\nAI recommendation\n\342\206\223\nScope Cutter\n\342\206\223\nJudge Mode\n\342\206\223\nLaunch\n\nTest invalid AI responses.\n\nTest Gemini failure.\n\nTest rate limiting.\n\nTest page refresh.\n\nMake sure existing deterministic features continue working when Gemini is unavailable.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL GOAL\n==========\n\nHALFTIME should now have two layers:\n\nDETERMINISTIC ENGINE\n\n* countdown\n* time calculations\n* task state\n* scope calculations\n* project health\n* progress\n* launch checklist\n\nAI ENGINE\n\n* idea reasoning\n* idea evaluation\n* MVP planning\n* next-action recommendations\n* scope recommendations\n* judge simulation\n* pitch coaching\n\nThe AI provides intelligence.\n\nThe application provides control.\n\nDo not redesign the product.\n\nImplement the Gemini intelligence layer into the existing HALFTIME application."
    items {
      text: "Continue working on the EXISTING HALFTIME application.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n* Do NOT redesign the UI.\n* Do NOT change the current theme, colors, layout, logo, animations, or navigation.\n* Do NOT rebuild the application.\n* Do NOT remove existing functionality.\n* Preserve everything that currently works.\n\nThe goal of this step is to connect HALFTIME to the Gemini API safely and add real AI reasoning to the existing product.\n\n==================================================\n\n1. GEMINI ARCHITECTURE\n   ==================================================\n\nUse Gemini through a SERVER-SIDE API route.\n\nThe Gemini API key must NEVER be exposed in client-side code.\n\nUse an environment variable:\n\nGEMINI_API_KEY\n\nFrontend:\nUser action\n\342\206\223\nHALFTIME server/API route\n\342\206\223\nGemini\n\342\206\223\nStructured JSON\n\342\206\223\nFrontend\n\342\206\223\nUI update\n\nDo NOT call Gemini directly from browser/client code.\n\n==================================================\n2. CREATE ONE REUSABLE AI SERVICE\n=================================\n\nCreate a centralized Gemini service/module.\n\nCreate reusable functions:\n\ngenerateIdeas()\nevaluateIdea()\ngenerateMVP()\nrecommendNextAction()\nrecommendScopeCuts()\njudgeProject()\nimprovePitch()\n\nDo not duplicate Gemini API initialization throughout the application.\n\nKeep the AI layer modular so the Gemini model can be changed later.\n\n==================================================\n3. STRUCTURED OUTPUT\n====================\n\nDo NOT depend on free-form Gemini text.\n\nAsk Gemini to return structured JSON.\n\nFor example, an idea evaluation should return:\n\n{\n\"verdict\": \"BUILD\",\n\"overallScore\": 8.6,\n\"innovation\": 8.8,\n\"problemFit\": 9.2,\n\"usability\": 8.1,\n\"execution\": 8.5,\n\"impact\": 8.0,\n\"feasibility\": 9.0,\n\"strengths\": [],\n\"weaknesses\": [],\n\"recommendations\": []\n}\n\nValidate the response before sending it to the frontend.\n\nIf the response is invalid, gracefully show an error rather than breaking the application.\n\n==================================================\n4. IDEA LAB \342\200\224 REAL AI\n=====================\n\nConnect the existing Idea Lab to Gemini.\n\nInputs:\n\nTeam skills\nPersonal frustrations\nInterests\nTarget users\nAvailable time\nHackathon category\nJudging criteria\n\nWhen the user clicks:\n\nGENERATE IDEAS\n\nSend the information to Gemini.\n\nAsk Gemini to generate exactly 3\342\200\2235 ideas.\n\nEach idea must contain:\n\nname\nproblem\ntargetUser\nsolution\ninnovationScore\nproblemFitScore\nfeasibilityScore\ndemoPotential\nverdict\n\nThe AI must NOT generate generic ideas.\n\nTell Gemini to prioritize:\n\n* real problems\n* clear users\n* hackathon feasibility\n* strong demo potential\n* originality\n* narrow MVP scope\n\nDisplay the results using the EXISTING Idea Card design.\n\nAdd loading state:\n\n\"HALFTIME IS THINKING...\"\n\nDo not create a chat interface.\n\n==================================================\n5. IDEA KILLER / IDEA EVALUATION\n================================\n\nConnect idea evaluation to Gemini.\n\nWhen a user selects an idea, send:\n\nidea\nproblem\ntarget user\nsolution\navailable time\nteam skills\nhackathon judging criteria\n\nAsk Gemini to critically evaluate it.\n\nImportant:\n\nGemini should NOT blindly praise the idea.\n\nIt must be allowed to return:\n\nBUILD\nMODIFY\nKILL\n\nExample:\n\nKILL:\n\n\"This solves a crowded problem without enough differentiation.\"\n\nMODIFY:\n\n\"Strong problem, but the target user is too broad.\"\n\nBUILD:\n\n\"Clear pain point, achievable MVP, and strong demo potential.\"\n\nDisplay:\n\nOverall score\nInnovation\nProblem Fit\nUsability\nExecution\nImpact\nFeasibility\n\nUse the existing visual components.\n\n==================================================\n6. MVP PLANNER \342\200\224 REAL AI\n========================\n\nWhen the user selects an idea and clicks:\n\nGENERATE MVP\n\nSend the selected idea and constraints to Gemini.\n\nReturn:\n\nproblemStatement\ntargetUser\ncoreSolution\nvalueProposition\n\nfeatures:\n\nmustBuild[]\nshouldBuild[]\nniceToHave[]\ncut[]\n\nAlso return estimated build time.\n\nThe most important instruction:\n\nThe MVP must be achievable within the user\'s remaining hackathon time.\n\nDo not generate huge feature lists.\n\nThe AI should aggressively control scope.\n\nDisplay the result in the existing MVP Planner.\n\n==================================================\n7. NEXT ACTION RECOMMENDATION\n=============================\n\nConnect the dashboard\'s:\n\nHALFTIME SAYS\n\nto Gemini.\n\nGive Gemini the current project state:\n\ntime remaining\nwork remaining\ntasks\nteam members\ncurrent project\nfeatures\nproject health\nrisk status\n\nAsk:\n\n\"What is the single most valuable thing this team should do next?\"\n\nReturn:\n\nnextAction\npriority\nestimatedTime\nreason\nrisk\nalternativeAction\n\nExample:\n\n{\n\"nextAction\": \"Finish the core AI evaluation flow\",\n\"priority\": \"CRITICAL\",\n\"estimatedTime\": \"1h 20m\",\n\"reason\": \"Everything else depends on this workflow.\"\n}\n\nDisplay this inside the EXISTING AI recommendation component.\n\nDo not redesign it.\n\n==================================================\n8. SCOPE CUTTER \342\200\224 AI RECOMMENDATIONS\n====================================\n\nKeep the existing deterministic Scope Cutter.\n\nThe existing application already knows:\n\nfeature\nestimatedTime\ndependencies\npriority\n\nNow add Gemini reasoning.\n\nSend Gemini:\n\nproject\nfeatures\nremainingTime\nremainingWork\njudgingCriteria\n\nAsk Gemini:\n\n\"Which features should this team cut first while preserving the project\'s core value and judging potential?\"\n\nGemini should return:\n\nfeature\nreason\ntimeSaved\nimpact\nrecommendation\n\nExample:\n\nAnalytics:\nCUT\n\nReason:\n\"Consumes 2 hours but does not improve the core demo.\"\n\nTeam profiles:\nCUT\n\nReason:\n\"Not required for the primary user journey.\"\n\nDark mode customization:\nCUT\n\nReason:\n\"Visual polish is less valuable than completing the core workflow.\"\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nGemini recommends.\n\nThe application\'s normal logic performs the actual time calculations.\n\nDo NOT allow Gemini to directly modify project state.\n\n==================================================\n9. JUDGE MODE \342\200\224 REAL AI\n=======================\n\nConnect Judge Mode to Gemini.\n\nUse these exact judging weights:\n\nInnovation & originality \342\200\224 25%\nProblem-solution fit \342\200\224 20%\nUsability & design \342\200\224 20%\nExecution & craft \342\200\224 15%\nImpact & storytelling \342\200\224 10%\nFeasibility & scale \342\200\224 10%\n\nAsk Gemini to act as a skeptical hackathon judge.\n\nInput:\n\nproblem\ntargetUser\nsolution\nfeatures\ntechnical implementation\ndemo flow\nimpact\n\nReturn:\n\ninnovation\nproblemFit\nusability\nexecution\nimpact\nfeasibility\noverallScore\nbiggestWeakness\nwhyYouMightLose\nimprovements[]\n\nDo not make the judge overly positive.\n\nThe most useful feedback should be specific and uncomfortable.\n\nDisplay:\n\nWHY YOU MIGHT LOSE\n\nThen:\n\nFIX BEFORE SUBMISSION\n\nUse the existing Judge Mode design.\n\n==================================================\n10. PITCH COACH\n===============\n\nIf Pitch Coach already exists, connect it to Gemini.\n\nGenerate:\n\nProblem\nWhy it matters\nSolution\nHow it works\nDemo moment\nImpact\nWhy now\n\nAlso generate a concise 60\342\200\22390 second pitch.\n\nKeep the output structured.\n\n==================================================\n11. AI ERROR HANDLING\n=====================\n\nThis is essential for public launch.\n\nHandle:\n\nAPI failure\ntimeout\nrate limit\ninvalid JSON\nempty response\nnetwork error\n\nNever show:\n\n500 Internal Server Error\n\nInstead show:\n\n\"HALFTIME AI is temporarily unavailable.\"\n\nThen:\n\n\"Your project data is safe. Try again in a moment.\"\n\nThe dashboard, timer, tasks, Scope Cutter calculations and saved project state must continue working without Gemini.\n\n==================================================\n12. LOADING STATES\n==================\n\nUse the existing visual language.\n\nDuring AI generation:\n\nHALFTIME IS THINKING...\n\nUse a subtle animation.\n\nFor idea generation:\n\nAnalyzing team strengths...\nFinding real problems...\nTesting feasibility...\nPreparing recommendations...\n\nDo not use fake long delays.\n\nKeep the loading experience short and professional.\n\n==================================================\n13. RATE LIMIT PROTECTION\n=========================\n\nProtect the Gemini endpoint.\n\nDo not allow unlimited anonymous requests.\n\nCreate a simple server-side rate limit.\n\nFor the MVP, use a reasonable per-user/IP request limit.\n\nIf the limit is reached, show:\n\n\"You\'ve reached the current AI usage limit. Try again later.\"\n\nDo not expose API details.\n\n==================================================\n14. SECURITY\n============\n\nNever expose:\n\nGEMINI_API_KEY\n\nto:\n\nwindow\nlocalStorage\nclient JavaScript\npublic environment variables\n\nOnly use it server-side.\n\nDo not log the API key.\n\nDo not send secrets to Gemini.\n\n==================================================\n15. MOCK FALLBACK\n=================\n\nCreate a fallback mock response for development/testing.\n\nIf Gemini is unavailable in development, the UI can use mock AI responses.\n\nClearly structure this so production can disable the mock fallback if desired.\n\n==================================================\n16. DO NOT CHANGE EXISTING UI\n=============================\n\nThis is critical.\n\nKeep:\n\n* current colors\n* current typography\n* current logo\n* current layout\n* current sidebar\n* current animations\n* current dashboard\n* current Scope Cutter\n* current navigation\n\nOnly connect real AI behind the existing interface.\n\n==================================================\n17. TEST THE FULL FLOW\n======================\n\nAfter implementation, test:\n\nIDEA LAB\n\342\206\223\nGenerate ideas\n\342\206\223\nSelect idea\n\342\206\223\nEvaluate idea\n\342\206\223\nGenerate MVP\n\342\206\223\nCreate features\n\342\206\223\nDashboard\n\342\206\223\nAI recommendation\n\342\206\223\nScope Cutter\n\342\206\223\nJudge Mode\n\342\206\223\nLaunch\n\nTest invalid AI responses.\n\nTest Gemini failure.\n\nTest rate limiting.\n\nTest page refresh.\n\nMake sure existing deterministic features continue working when Gemini is unavailable.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL GOAL\n==========\n\nHALFTIME should now have two layers:\n\nDETERMINISTIC ENGINE\n\n* countdown\n* time calculations\n* task state\n* scope calculations\n* project health\n* progress\n* launch checklist\n\nAI ENGINE\n\n* idea reasoning\n* idea evaluation\n* MVP planning\n* next-action recommendations\n* scope recommendations\n* judge simulation\n* pitch coaching\n\nThe AI provides intelligence.\n\nThe application provides control.\n\nDo not redesign the product.\n\nImplement the Gemini intelligence layer into the existing HALFTIME application."
    }
  }
}
