  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining API Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the server-side API architecture. I\'m considering reusable AI service functions, specifically `POST /api/ai/generate-ideas` and `POST /api/ai/evaluate-idea`. These functions will reside in `server/geminiService.ts` or `server.ts` routes, for both server and client.\n\n\n**Expanding API Capabilities**\n\nI\'ve expanded the API with new endpoints: `POST /api/ai/generate-mvp`, `POST /api/ai/recommend-next-action`, `POST /api/ai/recommend-scope-cuts`, `POST /api/ai/judge-project`, and `POST /api/ai/pitch-coach`.  These will have corresponding client-side functions in `src/services/aiService.ts`. I\'m also planning rate limiting (in-memory, IP-based) on the server to prevent abuse. Robust error handling is essential, including fallback data or graceful errors if Gemini fails.\n\n\n**Implementing Fallback Strategies**\n\nI\'m now implementing robust fallback data strategies for when Gemini is unavailable. The aim is a seamless user experience, never blocking them. I\'m focusing on strict model selection, using \'gemini-3.7-flash\' for standard tasks. I\'ll initialize `@google/genai` correctly, setting the API key, user agent, and requesting JSON responses with schema validation before sending the data back to the client.\n\n\n**Refining AI Service Functions**\n\nI\'m now consolidating the AI service functions into a more modular layer, so the underlying model can be easily swapped. My plan includes functions for idea generation, evaluation, MVP planning, next action recommendations, and scope cut suggestions. I\'m focusing on structured JSON output with schema validation and robust error handling. I\'m also ensuring the server handles the user interaction workflow with appropriate HALFTIME API calls, with Gemini providing the structured data.\n\n\n**Developing AI Workflow Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating AI-driven workflows for several key features. I\'m focusing on \"GENERATE AI MVP PLAN\" to trigger real Gemini synthesis, and \"RE-RUN JUDGE AUDIT\" to evaluate the project. The \"HALFTIME IS THINKING...\" loading state will be critical for a smooth user experience. I\'m also ensuring Gemini will be connected for \"HALFTIME SAYS\" / Next Move / Reasoning. I will work on integrating the functionality for the other features listed, such as pitch coaching.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 26703226
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
