  planner_response {
    response: "You should **never hardcode your API key directly into the code files**. \n\nInstead, in Google AI Studio, API keys and secrets are securely provided through the platform environment:\n\n1. **AI Studio Settings / Secrets Menu**:\n   - Go to the **Settings / Secrets** menu in the AI Studio interface.\n   - Add your secret under the variable name:\n     ```env\n     GEMINI_API_KEY\n     ```\n   - Paste your Gemini API key value there.\n\n2. **How the backend reads it**:\n   - The backend server (`server/geminiService.ts`) automatically reads this secret on the server side using:\n     ```ts\n     process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY\n     ```\n   - This ensures your key stays private on the server and is never exposed to the browser or in client-side code."
    modified_response: "You should **never hardcode your API key directly into the code files**. \n\nInstead, in Google AI Studio, API keys and secrets are securely provided through the platform environment:\n\n1. **AI Studio Settings / Secrets Menu**:\n   - Go to the **Settings / Secrets** menu in the AI Studio interface.\n   - Add your secret under the variable name:\n     ```env\n     GEMINI_API_KEY\n     ```\n   - Paste your Gemini API key value there.\n\n2. **How the backend reads it**:\n   - The backend server (`server/geminiService.ts`) automatically reads this secret on the server side using:\n     ```ts\n     process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY\n     ```\n   - This ensures your key stays private on the server and is never exposed to the browser or in client-side code."
