    user_response: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 STEP 4: VERIFY AND CONNECT THE AI TO THE PRODUCT\n\nIMPORTANT CONTEXT:\n\nThe Gemini API key is ALREADY configured securely in the project\'s Secrets settings as:\n\nGEMINI_API_KEY\n\nDo NOT ask me for the API key.\nDo NOT display it.\nDo NOT move it.\nDo NOT put it in client-side code.\nDo NOT create another API-key configuration.\n\nThe existing Gemini server-side architecture has already been implemented.\n\nNow verify that everything actually works end-to-end.\n\nDO NOT redesign the UI.\nDO NOT rebuild the application.\nDO NOT add unrelated features.\nPreserve all existing functionality and visual design.\n\n==================================================\n1. VERIFY GEMINI CONNECTION\n==================================================\n\nTest every existing AI capability:\n\n- Idea Generation\n- Idea Evaluation\n- MVP Generation\n- Next Action Recommendation\n- Scope Cutter Reasoning\n- Judge Simulation\n- Pitch Coach\n\nFor each verify:\n\nFrontend action\n\342\206\222 API request\n\342\206\222 server-side Gemini service\n\342\206\222 Gemini API\n\342\206\222 structured JSON\n\342\206\222 validation\n\342\206\222 frontend rendering\n\nIf something is broken, fix it.\n\nDo not rewrite working code.\n\n==================================================\n2. VERIFY API KEY SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nConfirm GEMINI_API_KEY is accessed ONLY server-side.\n\nSearch the project for accidental exposure.\n\nIt must NOT appear in:\n\n- React components\n- browser JavaScript\n- localStorage\n- sessionStorage\n- HTML\n- public environment variables\n- client-side configuration\n\nNever print the actual key.\n\n==================================================\n3. VERIFY STRUCTURED OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nEvery Gemini operation must:\n\n- validate JSON\n- handle missing fields\n- handle malformed responses\n- handle empty responses\n- handle API errors\n- handle timeouts\n- handle rate limits\n\nThe frontend must never crash because Gemini returns unexpected output.\n\n==================================================\n4. TEST IDEA LAB\n==================================================\n\nUse this demo input:\n\nTeam skills:\nFrontend development, AI, UI/UX\n\nFrustration:\nTeams waste too much time deciding what to build during hackathons.\n\nTarget users:\nHackathon teams\n\nAvailable time:\n10 hours\n\nGenerate 3\342\200\2235 ideas.\n\nEach must contain:\n\n- problem\n- target user\n- solution\n- scores\n- verdict\n- reasoning\n\nVerdicts must support:\n\nBUILD\nMODIFY\nKILL\n\n==================================================\n5. TEST IDEA EVALUATION\n==================================================\n\nSelect an idea and evaluate it.\n\nShow:\n\nInnovation\nProblem Fit\nUsability\nExecution\nImpact\nFeasibility\nOverall Score\n\nAlso show:\n\nWHY THIS COULD WIN\nWHY THIS COULD FAIL\nWHAT TO CHANGE\n\nThe evaluation must be specific.\n\nDo not allow generic AI praise.\n\n==================================================\n6. TEST MVP PLANNER\n==================================================\n\nGenerate an MVP from the selected idea.\n\nReturn:\n\nMUST BUILD\nSHOULD BUILD\nNICE TO HAVE\nCUT\n\nAlso return:\n\nEstimated build time.\n\nThe MVP must respect the team\'s remaining time.\n\n==================================================\n7. TEST DASHBOARD RECOMMENDATION\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\nRECALCULATE PLAN\n\nSend the CURRENT project state to Gemini:\n\n- time remaining\n- work remaining\n- tasks\n- features\n- project health\n- risk status\n- team\n- project goal\n\nReturn ONE primary recommendation.\n\nExample:\n\nFINISH CORE AI EVALUATION\n\nInclude:\n\naction\npriority\nestimated time\nreason\nrisk\n\nDo not return a giant list.\n\n==================================================\n8. CONNECT AI TO SCOPE CUTTER\n==================================================\n\nGemini recommends.\n\nThe USER decides.\n\nThe APPLICATION calculates.\n\nFlow:\n\nProject state\n\342\206\223\nGemini analysis\n\342\206\223\nRecommended cuts\n\342\206\223\nUser selects features\n\342\206\223\nApplication updates state\n\342\206\223\nDashboard recalculates\n\nGemini must NOT directly modify project state.\n\n==================================================\n9. VERIFY SCOPE CUTTER\n==================================================\n\nInitial state:\n\nTIME LEFT\n11h\n\nWORK\n14h\n\nSTATUS\nAT RISK\n\nGemini recommendation:\n\nAnalytics dashboard\n\342\210\2222h\n\nTeam profiles\n\342\210\2221h\n\nDark mode customization\n\342\210\22245m\n\nAfter selecting all three and clicking:\n\nCUT SELECTED\n\nThe application must calculate:\n\nWORK:\n10h 15m\n\nTIME LEFT:\n11h\n\nBUFFER:\n45m\n\nSTATUS:\nON TRACK\n\nUpdate:\n\n- project health\n- work remaining\n- capacity gap\n- scope\n- risk status\n\nShow:\n\n\"3h 45m recovered. You\'re back on track.\"\n\nDo NOT use Gemini to calculate these numbers.\n\n==================================================\n10. TEST JUDGE MODE\n==================================================\n\nEvaluate using:\n\nInnovation \342\200\224 25%\nProblem Fit \342\200\224 20%\nUsability \342\200\224 20%\nExecution \342\200\224 15%\nImpact \342\200\224 10%\nFeasibility \342\200\224 10%\n\nReturn:\n\nOverall Score\nWHY YOU MIGHT LOSE\nTOP 3 RISKS\nFIX BEFORE SUBMISSION\n\nMake the judge skeptical and specific.\n\n==================================================\n11. TEST PITCH COACH\n==================================================\n\nGenerate:\n\nProblem\nWhy it matters\nSolution\nHow it works\nDemo moment\nImpact\nWhy now\n\nThen generate a natural 60\342\200\22390 second pitch.\n\n==================================================\n12. TEST FAILURE HANDLING\n==================================================\n\nSimulate Gemini being unavailable.\n\nVerify:\n\nDashboard still works.\nCountdown still works.\nTasks still 