  user_input {
    user_response: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 STEP 5: PRODUCTION HARDENING & DEMO READINESS\n\nThe core application is now working and Gemini integration has been verified.\n\nDo NOT add new product features.\nDo NOT redesign the application.\nDo NOT change the visual identity.\nDo NOT rebuild working components.\n\nYour goal is to make the existing HALFTIME application reliable enough for a public hackathon launch and a live judging demo.\n\n==================================================\n1. RUN A PRODUCTION BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun the complete production build.\n\nCheck:\n\n- TypeScript\n- frontend compilation\n- backend compilation\n- API routes\n- imports\n- environment variables\n- production startup\n- client/server boundaries\n\nFix any issues found.\n\nDo not rewrite working architecture.\n\n==================================================\n2. TEST THE GOLDEN DEMO FLOW\n\nTest this exact flow:\n\nDashboard\n\342\206\222 Recalculate Plan\n\342\206\222 Gemini recommendation\n\342\206\222 Scope Cutter\n\342\206\222 Select Analytics\n\342\206\222 Select Team Profiles\n\342\206\222 Select Dark Mode\n\342\206\222 Cut Selected\n\342\206\222 Dashboard updates\n\342\206\222 Judge Mode\n\342\206\222 Judge feedback\n\342\206\222 Launch/Pitch Coach\n\nThe complete flow must work without refresh.\n\n==================================================\n3. TEST GEMINI FAILURE\n\nTemporarily simulate:\n\n- API timeout\n- API failure\n- invalid response\n- rate limit\n\nVerify the application gracefully falls back to:\n\n\"HALFTIME AI is temporarily unavailable.\"\n\nThe following MUST continue working:\n\n- countdown\n- navigation\n- tasks\n- project state\n- scope calculations\n- project health\n- launch checklist\n\n==================================================\n4. PREVENT DEMO BREAKAGE\n\nMake sure repeated clicks do not:\n\n- duplicate requests\n- duplicate tasks\n- double-apply scope cuts\n- corrupt project state\n- create duplicate activity events\n- start multiple timers\n\nDisable buttons appropriately while an AI request is running.\n\nShow a professional loading state.\n\n==================================================\n5. REFRESH TEST\n\nTest refreshing every major page:\n\nDashboard\nIdea Lab\nMVP Planner\nTasks\nResources\nJudge Mode\nLaunch\n\nMake sure the application does not crash.\n\nIf state persistence already exists, verify it.\n\nIf persistence does not exist, do NOT build a large persistence system now.\n\n==================================================\n6. MOBILE CHECK\n\nCheck:\n\n375px\n768px\n1440px\n\nFix only genuine layout problems.\n\nEnsure:\n\n- no horizontal scrolling\n- text does not overflow\n- buttons remain accessible\n- Scope Cutter remains usable\n- countdown remains visible\n- navigation works\n\nDo not redesign desktop.\n\n==================================================\n7. ACCESSIBILITY BASICS\n\nCheck:\n\n- keyboard navigation\n- visible focus states\n- button labels\n- sufficient text contrast\n- form labels\n- meaningful aria labels where necessary\n\nDo not sacrifice the visual design.\n\n==================================================\n8. PUBLIC LAUNCH SAFETY\n\nSearch for accidental exposure of:\n\n- API keys\n- secrets\n- internal credentials\n- debug information\n\nRemove console logs that expose sensitive information.\n\nDo not expose Gemini API credentials.\n\n==================================================\n9. LOADING / EMPTY / ERROR STATES\n\nEvery AI action should have:\n\nLoading\nSuccess\nError\n\nEvery important page should have a sensible empty state.\n\nDo not leave blank screens.\n\n==================================================\n10. DEMO DATA\n\nPreserve this polished initial demo state:\n\nTEAM:\nDOOM\n\nHACKATHON:\nDoraHacks 2.0\n\nPROJECT:\nHackathon Copilot\n\nTIME LEFT:\n11h\n\nWORK:\n14h\n\nHEALTH:\n72%\n\nSTATUS:\nAT RISK\n\nDo not remove the demo data.\n\n==================================================\n11. PERFORMANCE\n\nLook for obvious performance problems:\n\n- unnecessary repeated API calls\n- infinite rendering\n- duplicated requests\n- huge assets\n- unnecessary dependencies\n- excessive animations\n\nFix only obvious issues.\n\nDo not perform a major architectural rewrite.\n\n==================================================\n12. FINAL REPORT\n\nAfter testing, report:\n\nBUILD STATUS\nAPI STATUS\nGEMINI STATUS\nDASHBOARD STATUS\nSCOPE CUTTER STATUS\nJUDGE MODE STATUS\nPITCH COACH STATUS\nMOBILE STATUS\nERROR HANDLING STATUS\nSECURITY STATUS\n\nThen list any remaining issues.\n\nIf everything passes, clearly state:\n\nREADY FOR DEPLOYMENT"
    items {
      text: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 STEP 5: PRODUCTION HARDENING & DEMO READINESS\n\nThe core application is now working and Gemini integration has been verified.\n\nDo NOT add new product features.\nDo NOT redesign the application.\nDo NOT change the visual identity.\nDo NOT rebuild working components.\n\nYour goal is to make the existing HALFTIME application reliable enough for a public hackathon launch and a live judging demo.\n\n==================================================\n1. RUN A PRODUCTION BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun the complete production build.\n\nCheck:\n\n- TypeScript\n- frontend compilation\n- backend compilation\n- API routes\n- imports\n- environment variables\n- production startup\n- client/server boundaries\n\nFix any issues found.\n\nDo not rewrite working architecture.\n\n==================================================\n2. TEST THE GOLDEN DEMO FLOW\n\nTest this exact flow:\n\nDashboard\n\342\206\222 Recalculate Plan\n\342\206\222 Gemini recommendation\n\342\206\222 Scope Cutter\n\342\206\222 Select Analytics\n\342\206\222 Select Team Profiles\n\342\206\222 Select Dark Mode\n\342\206\222 Cut Selected\n\342\206\222 Dashboard updates\n\342\206\222 Judge Mode\n\342\206\222 Judge feedback\n\342\206\222 Launch/Pitch Coach\n\nThe complete flow must work without refresh.\n\n==================================================\n3. TEST GEMINI FAILURE\n\nTemporarily simulate:\n\n- API timeout\n- API failure\n- invalid response\n- rate limit\n\nVerify the application gracefully falls back to:\n\n\"HALFTIME AI is temporarily unavailable.\"\n\nThe following MUST continue working:\n\n- countdown\n- navigation\n- tasks\n- project state\n- scope calculations\n- project health\n- launch checklist\n\n==================================================\n4. PREVENT DEMO BREAKAGE\n\nMake sure repeated clicks do not:\n\n- duplicate requests\n- duplicate tasks\n- double-apply scope cuts\n- corrupt project state\n- create duplicate activity events\n- start multiple timers\n\nDisable buttons appropriately while an AI request is running.\n\nShow a professional loading state.\n\n==================================================\n5. REFRESH TEST\n\nTest refreshing every major page:\n\nDashboard\nIdea Lab\nMVP Planner\nTasks\nResources\nJudge Mode\nLaunch\n\nMake sure the application does not crash.\n\nIf state persistence already exists, verify it.\n\nIf persistence does not exist, do NOT build a large persistence system now.\n\n==================================================\n6. MOBILE CHECK\n\nCheck:\n\n375px\n768px\n1440px\n\nFix only genuine layout problems.\n\nEnsure:\n\n- no horizontal scrolling\n- text does not overflow\n- buttons remain accessible\n- Scope Cutter remains usable\n- countdown remains visible\n- navigation works\n\nDo not redesign desktop.\n\n==================================================\n7. ACCESSIBILITY BASICS\n\nCheck:\n\n- keyboard navigation\n- visible focus states\n- button labels\n- sufficient text contrast\n- form labels\n- meaningful aria labels where necessary\n\nDo not sacrifice the visual design.\n\n==================================================\n8. PUBLIC LAUNCH SAFETY\n\nSearch for accidental exposure of:\n\n- API keys\n- secrets\n- internal credentials\n- debug information\n\nRemove console logs that expose sensitive information.\n\nDo not expose Gemini API credentials.\n\n==================================================\n9. LOADING / EMPTY / ERROR STATES\n\nEvery AI action should have:\n\nLoading\nSuccess\nError\n\nEvery important page should have a sensible empty state.\n\nDo not leave blank screens.\n\n==================================================\n10. DEMO DATA\n\nPreserve this polished initial demo state:\n\nTEAM:\nDOOM\n\nHACKATHON:\nDoraHacks 2.0\n\nPROJECT:\nHackathon Copilot\n\nTIME LEFT:\n11h\n\nWORK:\n14h\n\nHEALTH:\n72%\n\nSTATUS:\nAT RISK\n\nDo not remove the demo data.\n\n==================================================\n11. PERFORMANCE\n\nLook for obvious performance problems:\n\n- unnecessary repeated API calls\n- infinite rendering\n- duplicated requests\n- huge assets\n- unnecessary dependencies\n- excessive animations\n\nFix only obvious issues.\n\nDo not perform a major architectural rewrite.\n\n==================================================\n12. FINAL REPORT\n\nAfter testing, report:\n\nBUILD STATUS\nAPI STATUS\nGEMINI STATUS\nDASHBOARD STATUS\nSCOPE CUTTER STATUS\nJUDGE MODE STATUS\nPITCH COACH STATUS\nMOBILE STATUS\nERROR HANDLING STATUS\nSECURITY STATUS\n\nThen list any remaining issues.\n\nIf everything passes, clearly state:\n\nREADY FOR DEPLOYMENT"
    }
  }
}
