  user_input {
    user_response: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 VERCEL DEPLOYMENT PREPARATION\n\nThe local production build now succeeds successfully.\n\nCurrent build:\n\nVite frontend \342\206\222 dist/\nExpress backend \342\206\222 dist/server.cjs\n\nThe project uses:\n\n- Vite\n- React\n- Node/Express\n- /api/health\n- /api/ai/*\n- Gemini server-side service\n- GEMINI_API_KEY through process.env\n\nI want to deploy this application to Vercel.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT redesign the UI.\nDo NOT change product functionality.\nDo NOT replace the existing architecture unnecessarily.\nDo NOT expose GEMINI_API_KEY.\nDo NOT remove the existing /api/ai/* functionality.\n\nInspect the existing project and determine the correct Vercel deployment configuration for this Vite + Express application.\n\nSpecifically verify:\n\n1. How the Express server should run on Vercel.\n2. Whether a vercel.json file is required.\n3. Whether the current server.ts needs a minimal Vercel-compatible export.\n4. Whether /api/health will work after deployment.\n5. Whether /api/ai/* will work after deployment.\n6. Whether the Vite SPA routes will work after deployment.\n7. Whether the frontend can correctly call the production API.\n8. Whether CORS configuration needs adjustment.\n9. Whether the existing dist/server.cjs build should remain or change.\n10. Whether GEMINI_API_KEY will correctly resolve from process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY.\n\nMake ONLY the minimum necessary changes for Vercel compatibility.\n\nDo NOT deploy.\n\nAfter making any required changes:\n\n1. Run npm run build.\n2. Verify the build succeeds.\n3. Explain exactly what Vercel configuration was added or changed.\n\nDo not ask me for the Gemini API key. It is already configured securely in the environment/secrets system."
    items {
      text: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 VERCEL DEPLOYMENT PREPARATION\n\nThe local production build now succeeds successfully.\n\nCurrent build:\n\nVite frontend \342\206\222 dist/\nExpress backend \342\206\222 dist/server.cjs\n\nThe project uses:\n\n- Vite\n- React\n- Node/Express\n- /api/health\n- /api/ai/*\n- Gemini server-side service\n- GEMINI_API_KEY through process.env\n\nI want to deploy this application to Vercel.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT redesign the UI.\nDo NOT change product functionality.\nDo NOT replace the existing architecture unnecessarily.\nDo NOT expose GEMINI_API_KEY.\nDo NOT remove the existing /api/ai/* functionality.\n\nInspect the existing project and determine the correct Vercel deployment configuration for this Vite + Express application.\n\nSpecifically verify:\n\n1. How the Express server should run on Vercel.\n2. Whether a vercel.json file is required.\n3. Whether the current server.ts needs a minimal Vercel-compatible export.\n4. Whether /api/health will work after deployment.\n5. Whether /api/ai/* will work after deployment.\n6. Whether the Vite SPA routes will work after deployment.\n7. Whether the frontend can correctly call the production API.\n8. Whether CORS configuration needs adjustment.\n9. Whether the existing dist/server.cjs build should remain or change.\n10. Whether GEMINI_API_KEY will correctly resolve from process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY.\n\nMake ONLY the minimum necessary changes for Vercel compatibility.\n\nDo NOT deploy.\n\nAfter making any required changes:\n\n1. Run npm run build.\n2. Verify the build succeeds.\n3. Explain exactly what Vercel configuration was added or changed.\n\nDo not ask me for the Gemini API key. It is already configured securely in the environment/secrets system."
