  planner_response {
    response: "### Vercel Deployment Preparation Report\n\nThe application has been prepared for Vercel deployment while preserving the architecture, local build steps, and server-side Gemini security.\n\n---\n\n### Verification of the 10 Deployment Requirements\n\n1. **How the Express server runs on Vercel**:\n   - On Vercel, server-side Express apps run as Serverless Functions rather than long-running `app.listen()` daemon processes.\n   - An `/api/index.ts` entrypoint was added that exports the Express app instance (`export default app`). Vercel\'s Node runtime delegates all incoming `/api/*` HTTP requests directly to this handler.\n   - In local and container environments (e.g. AI Studio, Docker, Cloud Run), `server.ts` automatically detects it is not on Vercel (`!process.env.VERCEL`) and binds to port `3000` as before.\n\n2. **`vercel.json` Configuration**:\n   - Created `vercel.json` at the root with standard rewrites:\n     - Routes `/api/(.*)` requests to the `/api` serverless function.\n     - Routes all other traffic to `/index.html` so client-side SPA routing and page refreshes work seamlessly.\n     - Sets `buildCommand: \"npm run build\"` and `outputDirectory: \"dist\"`.\n\n3. **`server.ts` Vercel-Compatible Export**:\n   - `server.ts` now exports `app` (`export { app }; export default app;`).\n   - The `startServer()` listener is guarded by `if (!process.env.VERCEL) { startServer(); }` to prevent port-binding conflicts in serverless function execution while keeping local/container startup intact.\n\n4. **`/api/health` Endpoint**:\n   - **Verified**: Returns `{ status: \"ok\", geminiConfigured: Boolean(process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY) }`.\n\n5. **`/api/ai/*` Endpoints**:\n   - **Verified**: All 7 server-side routes (`generate-ideas`, `evaluate-idea`, `generate-mvp`, `recommend-next-action`, `recommend-scope-cuts`, `judge-project`, `pitch-coach`) are mounted and handled identically by the serverless function.\n\n6. **Vite SPA Routes**:\n   - **Verified**: Static frontend assets are built to `dist/`. The `vercel.json` rewrite (`/(.*)` \342\206\222 `/index.html`) guarantees direct URL access and reloads work without 404 errors.\n\n7. **Frontend API Calls**:\n   - **Verified**: All client requests in `src/services/aiService.ts` use relative paths (`/api/health`, `/api/ai/...`). Since Vercel serves the static frontend and the `/api` functions from the same domain, relative fetches work automatically in both preview and production deployments.\n\n8. **CORS Configuration**:\n   - Added standard security headers (`X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options`) in Express. Same-origin requests work natively without CORS hurdles.\n\n9. **Existing `dist/server.cjs` Build**:\n   - **Preserved**: `npm run build` continues to execute `vite build && esbuild server.ts ...`, compiling both the `dist/` static files (used by Vercel and browsers) and `dist/server.cjs` (used by Docker/Node/Cloud Run).\n\n10. **`GEMINI_API_KEY` Resolution**:\n    - **Verified**: `server/geminiService.ts` accesses `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` on the server side. When deployed to Vercel, adding `GEMINI_API_KEY` in Vercel\'s **Project Settings \342\206\222 Environment Variables** will securely provide the key to the serverless function without exposing it to the browser.\n\n---\n\n### Files Added / Modified\n\n- **`vercel.json`** *(created)*:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"buildCommand\": \"npm run build\",\n    \"outputDirectory\": \"dist\",\n    \"rewrites\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"/api/(.*)\",\n        \"destination\": \"/api\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"/(.*)\",\n        \"destination\": \"/index.html\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n  ```\n- **`api/index.ts`** *(created)*:\n  ```ts\n  import app from \"../server.ts\";\n\n  export default app;\n  ```\n- **`server.ts`** *(updated)*:\n  - Added export for `app` (`export { app }; export default app;`).\n  - Added guard around `startServer()` for serverless environments (`if (!process.env.VERCEL) { startServer(); }`).\n\n---\n\n### Build Verification\n- **TypeScript Check**: `tsc --noEmit` passed cleanly.\n- **Production Build**: `npm run build` compiled both the frontend bundle (`dist/`) and the backend bundle (`dist/server.cjs`) with zero errors."
    modified_response: "### Vercel Deployment Preparation Report\n\nThe application has been prepared for Vercel deployment while preserving the architecture, local build steps, and server-side Gemini security.\n\n---\n\n### Verification of the 10 Deployment Requirements\n\n1. **How the Express server runs on Vercel**:\n   - On Vercel, server-side Express apps run as Serverless Functions rather than long-running `app.listen()` daemon processes.\n   - An `/api/index.ts` entrypoint was added that exports the Express app instance (`export default app`). Vercel\'s Node runtime delegates all incoming `/api/*` HTTP requests directly to this handler.\n   - In local and container environments (e.g. AI Studio, Docker, Cloud Run), `server.ts` automatically detects it is not on Vercel (`!process.env.VERCEL`) and binds to port `3000` as before.\n\n2. **`vercel.json` Configuration**:\n   - Created `vercel.json` at the root with standard rewrites:\n     - Routes `/api/(.*)` requests to the `/api` serverless function.\n     - Routes all other traffic to `/index.html` so client-side SPA routing and page refreshes work seamlessly.\n     - Sets `buildCommand: \"npm run build\"` and `outputDirectory: \"dist\"`.\n\n3. **`server.ts` Vercel-Compatible Export**:\n   - `server.ts` now exports `app` (`export { app }; export default app;`).\n   - The `startServer()` listener is guarded by `if (!process.env.VERCEL) { startServer(); }` to prevent port-binding conflicts in serverless function execution while keeping local/container startup intact.\n\n4. **`/api/health` Endpoint**:\n   - **Verified**: Returns `{ status: \"ok\", geminiConfigured: Boolean(process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY) }`.\n\n5. **`/api/ai/*` Endpoints**:\n   - **Verified**: All 7 server-side routes (`generate-ideas`, `evaluate-idea`, `generate-mvp`, `recommend-next-action`, `recommend-scope-cuts`, `judge-project`, `pitch-coach`) are mounted and handled identically by the serverless function.\n\n6. **Vite SPA Routes**:\n   - **Verified**: Static frontend assets are built to `dist/`. The `vercel.json` rewrite (`/(.*)` \342\206\222 `/index.html`) guarantees direct URL access and reloads work without 404 errors.\n\n7. **Frontend API Calls**:\n   - **Verified**: All client requests in `src/services/aiService.ts` use relative paths (`/api/health`, `/api/ai/...`). Since Vercel serves the static frontend and the `/api` functions from the same domain, relative fetches work automatically in both preview and production deployments.\n\n8. **CORS Configuration**:\n   - Added standard security headers (`X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options`) in Express. Same-origin requests work natively without CORS hurdles.\n\n9. **Existing `dist/server.cjs` Build**:\n   - **Preserved**: `npm run build` continues to execute `vite build && esbuild server.ts ...`, compiling both the `dist/` static files (used by Vercel and browsers) and `dist/server.cjs` (used by Docker/Node/Cloud Run).\n\n10. **`GEMINI_API_KEY` Resolution**:\n    - **Verified**: `server/geminiService.ts` accesses `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` on the server side. When deployed to Vercel, adding `GEMINI_API_KEY` in Vercel\'s **Project Settings \342\206\222 Environment Variables** will securely provide the key to the serverless function without exposing it to the browser.\n\n---\n\n### Files Added / Modified\n\n- **`vercel.json`** *(created)*:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"buildCommand\": \"npm run build\",\n    \"outputDirectory\": \"dist\",\n    \"rewrites\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"/api/(.*)\",\n        \"destination\": \"/api\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"/(.*)\",\n        \"destination\": \"/index.html\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n  ```\n- **`api/index.ts`** *(created)*:\n  ```ts\n  import app from \"../server.ts\";\n\n  export default app;\n  ```\n- **`server.ts`** *(updated)*:\n  - Added export for `app` (`export { app }; export default app;`).\n  - Added guard around `startServer()` for serverless environments (`if (!process.env.VERCEL) { startServer(); }`).\n\n---\n\n### Build Verification\n- **TypeScript Check**: `tsc --noEmit` passed cleanly.\n- **Production Build**: `npm run build` compiled both the frontend bundle (`dist/`) and the backend bundle (`dist/server.cjs`) with zero errors."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
