    user_response: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 STEP 6: REPLACE DEMO DATA WITH REAL USER PROJECTS\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe current application is a successful demo build, but it currently displays hardcoded/default Team DOOM data.\n\nWe now need to convert it into a real multi-user production application.\n\nDO NOT redesign the existing UI.\n\nDO NOT remove any existing features.\n\nDO NOT rebuild the dashboard.\n\nDO NOT break Gemini integration.\n\nDO NOT change the existing visual identity.\n\nThe existing Team DOOM data must become DEMO DATA only, not the default state for every user.\n\n==================================================\n1. ADD A FIRST-TIME USER EXPERIENCE\n==================================================\n\nWhen a new user visits HALFTIME, do NOT immediately show:\n\nTeam DOOM\nHackathon Copilot\n11h\n14h\n72%\n\nInstead show a professional onboarding/create-project screen.\n\nHeading:\n\nWELCOME TO HALFTIME\n\nSubtitle:\n\nTurn your remaining hackathon time into a shipping plan.\n\nCollect:\n\nProject name\nHackathon name\nHackathon deadline\nProject description\n\nOptional:\n\nTeam name\nTeam members\nTeam skills\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\nCREATE MY HACKATHON\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\nTRY DEMO\n\n==================================================\n2. DEMO MODE\n==================================================\n\nKeep the existing Team DOOM project as a dedicated demo project.\n\nWhen the user selects:\n\nTRY DEMO\n\nload:\n\nTeam:\nDOOM\n\nHackathon:\nDoraHacks 2.0\n\nProject:\nHackathon Copilot\n\nUse the existing demo values.\n\nDo NOT make this the default project for new users.\n\nClearly indicate:\n\nDEMO MODE\n\n==================================================\n3. PERSIST PROJECT DATA\n==================================================\n\nIntegrate the existing application with Supabase.\n\nCreate the minimum necessary database structure for:\n\nprojects\nteam_members\ntasks\nfeatures\nactivities\n\nProjects must contain at least:\n\nid\nname\nhackathon_name\ndescription\ndeadline\ncreated_at\nupdated_at\n\n==================================================\n4. PROJECT ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nEach project must have its own:\n\ntasks\nfeatures\nteam members\nactivity\nAI recommendations\nproject health\nscope state\n\nUser/project data must NEVER be globally shared.\n\nProject A must never see Project B\'s data.\n\n==================================================\n5. REAL DEADLINE CALCULATION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT store a hardcoded:\n\n\"11h remaining\"\n\nas the source of truth.\n\nStore the actual hackathon deadline.\n\nCalculate remaining time dynamically:\n\ndeadline - current time\n\nThe countdown must update continuously.\n\nIf the deadline passes:\n\nshow:\n\nHACKATHON ENDED\n\n==================================================\n6. REAL PROJECT HEALTH\n==================================================\n\nProject health must be calculated from the actual project\'s:\n\nremaining work\nremaining time\ntasks\nfeatures\nrisk\n\nDo not hardcode:\n\n72%\n\nThe existing deterministic project engine should calculate the value.\n\nPreserve the existing Scope Cutter logic.\n\n==================================================\n7. REAL TASKS AND FEATURES\n==================================================\n\nWhen a project is created, create an initial empty project.\n\nThe user should be able to add:\n\ntasks\nfeatures\n\nEach belongs to the current project.\n\nThe existing:\n\nTasks\nMVP Planner\nScope Cutter\nDashboard\n\nmust use the current project\'s database data.\n\n==================================================\n8. GEMINI CONTEXT\n\nWhen calling Gemini, send the CURRENT PROJECT DATA.\n\nGemini must NOT receive Team DOOM data unless the current project is the demo project.\n\nAI recommendations must be specific to:\n\ncurrent project\ncurrent tasks\ncurrent features\ncurrent deadline\ncurrent team\n\n==================================================\n9. DASHBOARD\n\nThe existing dashboard design is LOCKED.\n\nOnly replace hardcoded data with the current project\'s real data.\n\nKeep the existing:\n\n- health gauge\n- countdown\n- time/work comparison\n- AI recommendation\n- Scope Cutter\n- project signals\n- activity timeline\n\n==================================================\n10. PROJECT SWITCHING\n\nIf a user has multiple projects, provide a simple project switcher.\n\nExample:\n\nPROJECTS\n\nHackathon Copilot\nCampusShield\nEcoTrack\n\nSelecting a project loads only that project\'s data.\n\n==================================================\n11. NEW USER WITH NO PROJECT\n\nIf there is no project:\n\nshow onboarding.\n\nDo NOT show an empty Team DOOM dashboard.\n\n==================================================\n12. AUTHENTICATION\n\nUse the simplest reliable authentication supported by Supabase.\n\nA user should have an identity so their projects can be associated with them.\n\nDo not build custom authentication.\n\nUse Supabase authentication.\n\n==================================================\n13. SECURITY\n\nImplement appropriate Supabase Row Level Security.\n\nUsers must only access projects they are authorized to access.\n\nNever expose:\n\nSUPABASE service role key\nGEMINI API key\n\nto the browser.\n\nClient-side code may only use the appropriate public Supabase configuration.\n\n==================================================\n14. MIGRATION\n\nDo NOT delete the existing demo data.\n\nConvert it into a clearly identified demo project.\n\nExisting Team DOOM functionality must continue working.\n\n==================================================\n15. GOLDEN USER FLOW\n\nTest this:\n\nNew user\n\342\206\223\nOpen HALFTIME\n\342\206\223\nOnboarding\n\342\206\223\nEnter project\n\342\206\223\nEnter deadline\n\342\206\223\nCreate project\n\342\206\223\nDashboard\n\342\206\223\nAdd features\n\342\206\223\nAdd tasks\n\342\206\223\nDashboard calculates time/work\n\342\206\223\nGemini analyzes project\n\342\206\223\nScope Cutter recommends cuts\n\342\206\223\nUser cuts features\n\342\206\223\nProject health updates\n\342\206\223\nJudge Mode evaluates CURRENT project\n\342\206\223\nLaunch readiness uses CURRENT project\n\n==================================================\n16. DEMO FLOW\n\nAlso test:\n\nOpen HALFTIME\n\342\206\223\nTRY DEMO\n\342\206\223\nTeam DOOM project loads\n\342\206\223\nExisting golden-path demo works\n\n==================================================\n17. IMPORTANT\n\nDo not create a new dashboard.\n\nDo not redesign anything.\n\nDo not remove Team DOOM.\n\nDo not hardcode user data.\n\nReplace demo-only data with persistent project data.\n\nThe goal is:\n\nDEMO APPLICATION\n\342\206\222\nREAL MULTI-USER APPLICATION\n\nAfter implementation:\n\n1. Run the production build.\n2. Verify Supabase connection.\n3. Verify authentication.\n4. Verify project creation.\n5. Verify project isolation.\n6. Verify deadline calculation.\n7. Verify tasks/features.\n8. Verify Gemini receives current project data.\n9. Verify Scope Cutter.\n10. Verify Team DOOM demo mode.\n\nReport exactly what was implemented and any remaining limitations."
    items {
      text: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 STEP 6: REPLACE DEMO DATA WITH REAL USER PROJECTS\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe current application is a successful demo build, but it currently displays hardcoded/default Team DOOM data.\n\nWe now need to convert it into a real multi-user production application.\n\nDO NOT redesign the existing UI.\n\nDO NOT remove any existing features.\n\nDO NOT rebuild the dashboard.\n\nDO NOT break Gemini integration.\n\nDO NOT change the existing visual identity.\n\nThe existing Team DOOM data must become DEMO DATA only, not the default state for every user.\n\n==================================================\n1. ADD A FIRST-TIME USER EXPERIENCE\n==================================================\n\nWhen a new user visits HALFTIME, do NOT immediately show:\n\nTeam DOOM\nHackathon Copilot\n11h\n14h\n72%\n\nInstead show a professional onboarding/create-project screen.\n\nHeading:\n\nWELCOME TO HALFTIME\n\nSubtitle:\n\nTurn your remaining hackathon time into a shipping plan.\n\nCollect:\n\nProject name\nHackathon name\nHackathon deadline\nProject description\n\nOptional:\n\nTeam name\nTeam members\nTeam skills\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\nCREATE MY HACKATHON\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\nTRY DEMO\n\n==================================================\n2. DEMO MODE\n==================================================\n\nKeep the existing Team DOOM project as a dedicated demo project.\n\nWhen the user selects:\n\nTRY DEMO\n\nload:\n\nTeam:\nDOOM\n\nHackathon:\nDoraHacks 2.0\n\nProject:\nHackathon Copilot\n\nUse the existing demo values.\n\nDo NOT make this the default project for new users.\n\nClearly indicate:\n\nDEMO MODE\n\n==================================================\n3. PERSIST PROJECT DATA\n==================================================\n\nIntegrate the existing application with Supabase.\n\nCreate the minimum necessary database structure for:\n\nprojects\nteam_members\ntasks\nfeatures\nactivities\n\nProjects must contain at least:\n\nid\nname\nhackathon_name\