  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Metrics**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how `projectEngine.ts` will calculate project metrics, specifically for dynamic deadlines and actual tasks. For the Team DOOM demo project, the baseline time available is 11 hours (or the dynamic deadline if it is set), and this appears to be the most relevant thing to start with.\n\n\n**Calculating Project Health**\n\nI\'ve been calculating project health based on work remaining and time available, as the key metric. The system now uses a `capacityGapMinutes` calculation to determine status: \'at-risk\' for work exceeding available time, and \'on-track\' if time allows. Severity determines \'at-risk\' scores (50-75%), and \'on-track\' scores reflect the buffer (85-98%). I\'m also planning to handle projects with no initial tasks.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 281180054
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
