  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Supabase Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the Supabase architecture. I\'m focusing on the persistence layer, specifically `src/lib/supabase.ts`. This file will handle the initialization of the Supabase client. I\'m checking for the necessary environment variables, `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, and using them to create the client if present.\n\n\n**Abstracting Persistence Layer**\n\nI\'ve been working on a clean storage abstraction. I\'m focusing on `supabaseService.ts`, and I\'ve started building out functions for anonymous user authentication, including session management. I\'m also planning the storage of projects, tasks, features, and activities to Supabase when online, and to localStorage when offline. I\'m also making sure to preserve the Team DOOM demo project.\n\n\n**Refining Hackathon Project UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user interface elements for project creation and management. I\'m finalizing details for a time picker or quick runway selector, incorporating a project description and optional team details. The primary CTA will be \'CREATE MY HACKATHON,\' with a secondary \'TRY DEMO\' option. I am also working on dynamic real deadline calculation and project health metrics.\n\n\n**Calculating Project Health Metrics**\n\nI\'m now incorporating real user tasks and deadlines. The system will calculate total work from uncompleted task estimates, then dynamically generate metrics. These include `workRequiredHours`, `timeAvailableHours`, `capacityGapHours`, `score`, and a project `status`. Scope Cutter recommendations will adapt based on the project\'s features and tasks. I also plan to provide Gemini with real project data. I\'m focusing on the SQL schema for Supabase.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 147029024
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
