steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787481367
      nanos: 870196077
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 FINAL PRODUCTIZATION: REMOVE ALL DUMMY FUNCTIONALITY\n\nThis is a critical implementation task.\n\nHALFTIME must become a genuinely usable multi-user application.\n\nI DO NOT WANT DUMMY FEATURES, FAKE AI RESPONSES, STATIC VALUES, PLACEHOLDER BUTTONS, OR VISUAL-ONLY INTERACTIONS IN THE NORMAL USER EXPERIENCE.\n\nDo NOT redesign the existing UI.\n\nDo NOT rebuild the application from scratch.\n\nPreserve the current professional visual design, navigation, animations, components, and working Gemini integration.\n\nYour job is to AUDIT THE ENTIRE APPLICATION and replace every dummy/static/placeholder behavior with real functionality.\n\n==================================================\nCORE RULE\n==================================================\n\nEvery visible:\n\n- button\n- input\n- card\n- metric\n- score\n- progress bar\n- timer\n- recommendation\n- task\n- feature\n- AI result\n- activity item\n- checklist item\n- project value\n\nmust either:\n\nA. come from real user/project state,\n\nB. be calculated by deterministic application logic,\n\nC. be generated by the real Gemini API,\n\nD. be persisted in Supabase,\n\nor\n\nE. be a real UI control that changes application/database state.\n\nThere must be NO fake functionality presented as real functionality.\n\n==================================================\n1. REMOVE GLOBAL DEMO DATA\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT show these as the default experience:\n\nTeam DOOM\nHackathon Copilot\n11h\n14h\n72%\n8.55\n\nThese belong ONLY to an explicit:\n\nTRY DEMO\n\nmode.\n\nA new user must start with their own project.\n\nIf a new user has no project:\n\nshow:\n\nWELCOME TO HALFTIME\n\nCreate your hackathon project.\n\n==================================================\n2. REAL USER AUTHENTICATION\n==================================================\n\nUse Supabase Authentication.\n\nImplement:\n\nSign up\nSign in\nSign out\nSession persistence\nCurrent user detection\n\nSupport a simple reliable authentication method.\n\nDo not create custom authentication.\n\nIf authentication is not yet configured, implement the required Supabase integration and clearly identify the required environment variables.\n\nNever expose the Supabase service-role key.\n\n==================================================\n3. REAL PROJECT CREATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate a real onboarding flow.\n\nCollect:\n\nProject name\nHackathon name\nHackathon deadline\nProject description\nTeam name\n\nAllow adding team members.\n\nWhen the user clicks:\n\nCREATE PROJECT\n\ncreate a real Supabase project record.\n\nDo not simply change local React state.\n\nAfter creation:\n\npersist the project\nload the project\nredirect to the dashboard\n\n==================================================\n4. REAL PROJECT ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nEvery piece of data must belong to a project.\n\nImplement relationships for:\n\nprojects\nteam_members\ntasks\nfeatures\nideas\nactivities\njudge_evaluations\nmvp_plans\nlaunch_items\n\nA user must NEVER see another user\'s project data.\n\nImplement appropriate Supabase Row Level Security.\n\n==================================================\n5. REAL DEADLINE\n==================================================\n\nNever hardcode:\n\n11h\n\nStore:\n\nhackathon_deadline\n\nCalculate:\n\ntimeRemaining = deadline - currentTime\n\nThe countdown must update continuously.\n\nHandle:\n\nnormal\nwarning\ncritical\ndeadline passed\n\nWhen the deadline passes:\n\nshow:\n\nHACKATHON ENDED\n\n==================================================\n6. REAL PROJECT HEALTH\n==================================================\n\nRemove hardcoded:\n\n72%\n\nProject health must be calculated from actual project data.\n\nUse:\n\nremaining work\nremaining time\ntask completion\nfeature scope\nrisk factors\n\nThe calculation must be deterministic.\n\nShow why the health score changed.\n\n==================================================\n7. REAL TASK MANAGEMENT\n==================================================\n\nTasks must be persisted.\n\nImplement:\n\nCreate task\nEdit task\nDelete task\nAssign task\nChange status\nChange priority\nSet estimated hours\nMark complete\n\nStatuses:\n\nBACKLOG\nTODO\nIN PROGRESS\nDONE\n\nEvery change must persist to Supabase.\n\nRefreshing the page must preserve the change.\n\n==================================================\n8. REAL TEAM ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nTeam members must come from the current project.\n\nAllow:\n\nAdd member\nEdit member\nRemove member\nAssign task to member\n\nDo not use hardcoded:\n\nBuilder\nDesigner\nGrowth\nProduct\n\nunless the user actually created those members.\n\n==================================================\n9. REAL IDEA LAB\n==================================================\n\nIdea Lab must use the REAL Gemini API.\n\nUser provides:\n\nskills\ninterests\nfrustrations\ntarget users\nhackathon criteria\navailable time\n\nGenerate 3\342\200\2235 ideas through Gemini.\n\nPersist generated ideas to Supabase.\n\nEach idea must include:\n\nname\nproblem\ntarget user\nsolution\ninnovation score\nproblem fit\nfeasibility\ndemo potential\nverdict\nreasoning\n\nAllow:\n\nSave idea\nDelete idea\nSelect idea\nEvaluate idea\n\nNo fake generated ideas in normal mode.\n\n==================================================\n10. REAL IDEA KILLER\n==================================================\n\nUse Gemini to evaluate the selected real project idea.\n\nReturn:\n\nBUILD\nMODIFY\nKILL\n\nInclude:\n\nInnovation\nProblem Fit\nUsability\nExecution\nImpact\nFeasibility\nOverall score\n\nPersist evaluation results.\n\nShow:\n\nWHY THIS COULD WIN\nWHY THIS COULD FAIL\nWHAT TO CHANGE\n\nThe evaluation must use the actual selected idea.\n\n==================================================\n11. REAL PROBLEM STATEMENT GENERATOR\n==================================================\n\nAdd a real action:\n\nDEFINE THE PROBLEM\n\nUse the actual project/idea.\n\nGemini should generate:\n\nProblem statement\nTarget user\nPain point\nCurrent alternative\nWhy existing solutions fail\nDesired outcome\nSuccess criteria\n\nAllow the user to:\n\nAccept\nEdit\nRegenerate\n\nPersist the accepted problem statement.\n\n==================================================\n12. REAL MVP GENERATOR\n==================================================\n\nUse Gemini on the actual selected idea.\n\nGenerate:\n\nMUST BUILD\nSHOULD BUILD\nNICE TO HAVE\nCUT\n\nAlso generate:\n\nEstimated total build time\nRecommended MVP workflow\nCore demo path\n\nPersist the MVP plan.\n\nAllow the user to edit the generated features.\n\n==================================================\n13. REAL BUILD ROADMAP\n==================================================\n\nImplement a real:\n\nGENERATE BUILD ROADMAP\n\nUse:\n\nCurrent MVP\nFeatures\nTeam members\nAvailable time\nTask dependencies\n\nGenerate a realistic sequence.\n\nExample structure:\n\nPhase\nTask\nOwner\nEstimated time\nDependencies\nPriority\n\nPersist the generated roadmap.\n\nAllow converting roadmap items into real tasks.\n\n==================================================\n14. REAL TEAM TASK ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nWhen converting roadmap items into tasks:\n\nassign them to actual project members.\n\nPersist assignments.\n\nTask estimated time must contribute to:\n\nWORK REMAINING\n\n==================================================\n15. REAL SCOPE CUTTER\n==================================================\n\nThis is a core feature.\n\nGemini recommends cuts.\n\nThe USER chooses cuts.\n\nThe APPLICATION calculates the consequences.\n\nDo NOT allow Gemini to directly change the project.\n\nWhen a user cuts a feature:\n\npersist the feature state.\n\nRecalculate:\n\nremaining work\ncapacity gap\nproject health\nrisk\nscope score\n\nThe dashboard must immediately reflect the change.\n\n==================================================\n16. REAL RISK DETECTION\n==================================================\n\nRisk detection must use actual project data.\n\nAnalyze:\n\ndeadline\nremaining work\ntask completion\nunfinished critical tasks\nfeature count\nteam capacity\nblocked tasks\n\nProduce:\n\nrisk level\nrisk reasons\nrecommended action\n\nUse deterministic calculations for numerical risk.\n\nUse Gemini for explanation and recommendations.\n\n==================================================\n17. REAL AI RESOURCE MANAGER\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT pretend we have access to third-party credit balances unless an official API provides them.\n\nDo NOT display fake:\n\nGemini 78%\nClaude 84%\nBase44 41%\n\nInstead create a REAL resource manager where the user can add:\n\nTool\nResource type\nBudget/limit\nCurrent usage\nReset date\nNotes\n\nCalculate remaining budget from user-entered data.\n\nIf an official API integration exists and is configured, use it.\n\nOtherwise clearly label the values:\n\nUSER ENTERED\n\nNever present invented balances as real.\n\n==================================================\n18. REAL AI TOOL RECOMMENDER\n==================================================\n\nImplement:\n\nRECOMMEND A TOOL\n\nInput:\n\nTask\nTime available\nTeam skills\nExisting stack\nBudget/resource constraints\n\nUse Gemini to recommend the most appropriate tool or existing stack.\n\nReturn:\n\nRecommended tool\nWhy\nSetup cost\nEstimated time saved\nAlternative\n\nThe recommendation must consider the user\'s actual project.\n\n==================================================\n19. REAL PROJECT HEALTH DASHBOARD\n==================================================\n\nEvery dashboard metric must come from actual project state.\n\nNo hardcoded metrics.\n\nDisplay:\n\nTime remaining\nWork remaining\nCapacity gap\nTask completion\nScope\nProject health\nRisk\nMVP progress\n\nEvery metric must update when the underlying data changes.\n\n==================================================\n20. REAL JUDGE SIMULATOR\n==================================================\n\nUse the actual project.\n\nEvaluate:\n\nInnovation \342\200\224 25%\nProblem Fit \342\200\224 20%\nUsability \342\200\224 20%\nExecution \342\200\224 15%\nImpact \342\200\224 10%\nFeasibility \342\200\224 10%\n\nGenerate through Gemini:\n\nOverall score\nStrengths\nWeaknesses\nWhy you might lose\nTop risks\nFixes\n\nPersist the latest evaluation.\n\nDo not use static scores.\n\n==================================================\n21. REAL PITCH COACH\n==================================================\n\nUse the actual project.\n\nGenerate:\n\nProblem\nWhy it matters\nSolution\nHow it works\nDemo moment\nImpact\nWhy now\n\nGenerate a real 60\342\200\22390 second pitch.\n\nAllow:\n\nRegenerate\nEdit\nCopy\n\nPersist the user\'s final pitch.\n\n==================================================\n22. REAL DEMO FLOW GENERATOR\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nGENERATE DEMO FLOW\n\nGemini should use the actual:\n\nMVP\nfeatures\nproject\nuser journey\njudge criteria\n\nGenerate:\n\nOpening\nProblem\nSolution\nDemo steps\nWow moment\nTechnical explanation\nImpact\nClosing\n\nEstimate:\n\nDemo duration\n\nAllow the user to edit and save the final demo flow.\n\n==================================================\n23. REAL LAUNCH CHECKLIST\n==================================================\n\nCreate launch checklist items based on the actual project.\n\nExamples:\n\nMVP complete\nCritical bugs fixed\nDemo tested\nPitch complete\nREADME complete\nScreenshots\nDemo video\nSubmission\nRepository\nDeployment\n\nUsers can:\n\nAdd item\nEdit item\nComplete item\nDelete item\n\nPersist everything.\n\nCalculate:\n\nLAUNCH READINESS %\n\nfrom actual checklist completion.\n\nNever hardcode it.\n\n==================================================\n24. REAL ACTIVITY FEED\n==================================================\n\nActivity must come from actual events.\n\nExamples:\n\nProject created\nFeature added\nTask completed\nFeature cut\nAI evaluation completed\nMVP generated\nJudge evaluation completed\nPitch updated\n\nPersist activity.\n\nDo not use fake timestamps.\n\n==================================================\n25. REAL PROJECT SWITCHER\n==================================================\n\nIf a user has multiple projects:\n\nshow their actual projects.\n\nSelecting a project loads its real data.\n\nNo cross-project contamination.\n\n==================================================\n26. DEMO MODE\n==================================================\n\nKeep Team DOOM as an explicit demo.\n\nAdd:\n\nTRY DEMO\n\nDemo mode can use the existing polished Team DOOM data.\n\nClearly label:\n\nDEMO MODE\n\nNormal user mode must NEVER automatically load demo data.\n\n==================================================\n27. NO FAKE AI FALLBACKS IN PRODUCTION\n==================================================\n\nDevelopment may use mock responses only if explicitly enabled.\n\nProduction must NEVER silently replace Gemini output with fake AI responses.\n\nIf Gemini fails:\n\nshow:\n\nHALFTIME AI is temporarily unavailable.\n\nAllow:\n\nTRY AGAIN\n\nDo not fabricate an AI response.\n\n==================================================\n28. NO FAKE CREDIT DATA\n==================================================\n\nDo not invent third-party API usage.\n\nIf usage cannot be retrieved automatically:\n\nshow:\n\nUSER ENTERED\n\nor:\n\nNOT CONNECTED\n\nNever present fake numbers as real.\n\n==================================================\n29. DATABASE PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nAll important user state must survive:\n\nrefresh\nlogout/login\ndifferent device\nnew browser session\n\nPersist:\n\nprojects\nideas\nproblem statements\nMVPs\nfeatures\ntasks\nteam members\nroadmaps\nactivities\njudge evaluations\npitches\ndemo flows\nlaunch checklist\n\n==================================================\n30. LOADING / ERROR STATES\n==================================================\n\nEvery real operation needs:\n\nloading\nsuccess\nerror\n\nExamples:\n\nGenerating ideas...\nSaving project...\nEvaluating project...\nGenerating roadmap...\nSaving task...\n\nNever leave a button visually active while an operation is pending.\n\nPrevent duplicate submissions.\n\n==================================================\n31. SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nNever expose:\n\nGEMINI_API_KEY\nSupabase service-role key\n\nClient-side code may only use safe public configuration.\n\nImplement Row Level Security.\n\nValidate server-side inputs.\n\nNever trust project IDs supplied by the browser without authorization checks.\n\n==================================================\n32. FINAL AUDIT\n\nSearch the entire codebase for:\n\nmock\ndummy\nfake\nplaceholder\nhardcoded\nsample\ndemo\nTODO\nComing Soon\n\nFor every occurrence:\n\ndetermine whether it is:\n\nA. legitimate demo mode\n\nB. legitimate empty-state example\n\nC. actual fake functionality\n\nRemove or replace C.\n\nDo not remove legitimate demo mode.\n\n==================================================\n33. FEATURE COMPLETENESS TEST\n\nTest every feature from a brand-new account:\n\nCreate Project\n\342\206\223\nAdd Team\n\342\206\223\nDefine Problem\n\342\206\223\nGenerate Ideas\n\342\206\223\nEvaluate Idea\n\342\206\223\nGenerate MVP\n\342\206\223\nGenerate Roadmap\n\342\206\223\nCreate Tasks\n\342\206\223\nAssign Tasks\n\342\206\223\nTrack Countdown\n\342\206\223\nDetect Risk\n\342\206\223\nRecommend Tools\n\342\206\223\nManage Resources\n\342\206\223\nCut Scope\n\342\206\223\nUpdate Health\n\342\206\223\nJudge Project\n\342\206\223\nGenerate Pitch\n\342\206\223\nGenerate Demo Flow\n\342\206\223\nComplete Launch Checklist\n\nEvery step must use the CURRENT user\'s CURRENT project.\n\n==================================================\n34. PRODUCTION RULE\n\nThere must be NO dummy data in the normal production experience.\n\nIf a feature cannot be genuinely implemented:\n\nDO NOT fake it.\n\nInstead show a clear state such as:\n\nNOT CONNECTED\n\nor\n\nCONFIGURATION REQUIRED\n\nor remove the feature from the normal user flow until it is functional.\n\n==================================================\n35. FINAL VERIFICATION\n\nRun:\n\nnpm install\nnpm run build\n\nThen test:\n\n- new user\n- authentication\n- project creation\n- project persistence\n- project isolation\n- Gemini\n- tasks\n- features\n- Scope Cutter\n- countdown\n- risk detection\n- Judge Mode\n- Pitch Coach\n- Demo Flow\n- Launch Checklist\n- mobile\n- logout/login\n- refresh\n\nDo not report a feature as complete unless you actually verify its behavior.\n\nAt the end provide a table:\n\nFEATURE | REAL / PARTIAL / NOT IMPLEMENTED | HOW IT WORKS\n\nDo not claim success based only on source-code inspection.\n\nThe goal is:\n\nNO DUMMIES.\nNO FAKE AI.\nNO HARDCODED USER DATA.\nNO VISUAL-ONLY BUTTONS.\n\nHALFTIME must behave like a real application used by real people."
    items {
      text: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 FINAL PRODUCTIZATION: REMOVE ALL DUMMY FUNCTIONALITY\n\nThis is a critical implementation task.\n\nHALFTIME must become a genuinely usable multi-user application.\n\nI DO NOT WANT DUMMY FEATURES, FAKE AI RESPONSES, STATIC VALUES, PLACEHOLDER BUTTONS, OR VISUAL-ONLY INTERACTIONS IN THE NORMAL USER EXPERIENCE.\n\nDo NOT redesign the existing UI.\n\nDo NOT rebuild the application from scratch.\n\nPreserve the current professional visual design, navigation, animations, components, and working Gemini integration.\n\nYour job is to AUDIT THE ENTIRE APPLICATION and replace every dummy/static/placeholder behavior with real functionality.\n\n==================================================\nCORE RULE\n==================================================\n\nEvery visible:\n\n- button\n- input\n- card\n- metric\n- score\n- progress bar\n- timer\n- recommendation\n- task\n- feature\n- AI result\n- activity item\n- checklist item\n- project value\n\nmust either:\n\nA. come from real user/project state,\n\nB. be calculated by deterministic application logic,\n\nC. be generated by the real Gemini API,\n\nD. be persisted in Supabase,\n\nor\n\nE. be a real UI control that changes application/database state.\n\nThere must be NO fake functionality presented as real functionality.\n\n==================================================\n1. REMOVE GLOBAL DEMO DATA\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT show these as the default experience:\n\nTeam DOOM\nHackathon Copilot\n11h\n14h\n72%\n8.55\n\nThese belong ONLY to an explicit:\n\nTRY DEMO\n\nmode.\n\nA new user must start with their own project.\n\nIf a new user has no project:\n\nshow:\n\nWELCOME TO HALFTIME\n\nCreate your hackathon project.\n\n==================================================\n2. REAL USER AUTHENTICATION\n==================================================\n\nUse Supabase Authentication.\n\nImplement:\n\nSign up\nSign in\nSign out\nSession persistence\nCurrent user detection\n\nSupport a simple reliable authentication method.\n\nDo not create custom authentication.\n\nIf authentication is not yet configured, implement the required Supabase integration and clearly identify the required environment variables.\n\nNever expose the Supabase service-role key.\n\n==================================================\n3. REAL PROJECT CREATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate a real onboarding flow.\n\nCollect:\n\nProject name\nHackathon name\nHackathon deadline\nProject description\nTeam name\n\nAllow adding team members.\n\nWhen the user clicks:\n\nCREATE PROJECT\n\ncreate a real Supabase project record.\n\nDo not simply change local React state.\n\nAfter creation:\n\npersist the project\nload the project\nredirect to the dashboard\n\n==================================================\n4. REAL PROJECT ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nEvery piece of data must belong to a project.\n\nImplement relationships for:\n\nprojects\nteam_members\ntasks\nfeatures\nideas\nactivities\njudge_evaluations\nmvp_plans\nlaunch_items\n\nA user must NEVER see another user\'s project data.\n\nImplement appropriate Supabase Row Level Security.\n\n==================================================\n5. REAL DEADLINE\n==================================================\n\nNever hardcode:\n\n11h\n\nStore:\n\nhackathon_deadline\n\nCalculate:\n\ntimeRemaining = deadline - currentTime\n\nThe countdown must update continuously.\n\nHandle:\n\nnormal\nwarning\ncritical\ndeadline passed\n\nWhen the deadline passes:\n\nshow:\n\nHACKATHON ENDED\n\n==================================================\n6. REAL PROJECT HEALTH\n==================================================\n\nRemove hardcoded:\n\n72%\n\nProject health must be calculated from actual project data.\n\nUse:\n\nremaining work\nremaining time\ntask completion\nfeature scope\nrisk factors\n\nThe calculation must be deterministic.\n\nShow why the health score changed.\n\n==================================================\n7. REAL TASK MANAGEMENT\n==================================================\n\nTasks must be persisted.\n\nImplement:\n\nCreate task\nEdit task\nDelete task\nAssign task\nChange status\nChange priority\nSet estimated hours\nMark complete\n\nStatuses:\n\nBACKLOG\nTODO\nIN PROGRESS\nDONE\n\nEvery change must persist to Supabase.\n\nRefreshing the page must preserve the change.\n\n==================================================\n8. REAL TEAM ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nTeam members must come from the current project.\n\nAllow:\n\nAdd member\nEdit member\nRemove member\nAssign task to member\n\nDo not use hardcoded:\n\nBuilder\nDesigner\nGrowth\nProduct\n\nunless the user actually created those members.\n\n==================================================\n9. REAL IDEA LAB\n==================================================\n\nIdea Lab must use the REAL Gemini API.\n\nUser provides:\n\nskills\ninterests\nfrustrations\ntarget users\nhackathon criteria\navailable time\n\nGenerate 3\342\200\2235 ideas through Gemini.\n\nPersist generated ideas to Supabase.\n\nEach idea must include:\n\nname\nproblem\ntarget user\nsolution\ninnovation score\nproblem fit\nfeasibility\ndemo potential\nverdict\nreasoning\n\nAllow:\n\nSave idea\nDelete idea\nSelect idea\nEvaluate idea\n\nNo fake generated ideas in normal mode.\n\n==================================================\n10. REAL IDEA KILLER\n==================================================\n\nUse Gemini to evaluate the selected real project idea.\n\nReturn:\n\nBUILD\nMODIFY\nKILL\n\nInclude:\n\nInnovation\nProblem Fit\nUsability\nExecution\nImpact\nFeasibility\nOverall score\n\nPersist evaluation results.\n\nShow:\n\nWHY THIS COULD WIN\nWHY THIS COULD FAIL\nWHAT TO CHANGE\n\nThe evaluation must use the actual selected idea.\n\n==================================================\n11. REAL PROBLEM STATEMENT GENERATOR\n==================================================\n\nAdd a real action:\n\nDEFINE THE PROBLEM\n\nUse the actual project/idea.\n\nGemini should generate:\n\nProblem statement\nTarget user\nPain point\nCurrent alternative\nWhy existing solutions fail\nDesired outcome\nSuccess criteria\n\nAllow the user to:\n\nAccept\nEdit\nRegenerate\n\nPersist the accepted problem statement.\n\n==================================================\n12. REAL MVP GENERATOR\n==================================================\n\nUse Gemini on the actual selected idea.\n\nGenerate:\n\nMUST BUILD\nSHOULD BUILD\nNICE TO HAVE\nCUT\n\nAlso generate:\n\nEstimated total build time\nRecommended MVP workflow\nCore demo path\n\nPersist the MVP plan.\n\nAllow the user to edit the generated features.\n\n==================================================\n13. REAL BUILD ROADMAP\n==================================================\n\nImplement a real:\n\nGENERATE BUILD ROADMAP\n\nUse:\n\nCurrent MVP\nFeatures\nTeam members\nAvailable time\nTask dependencies\n\nGenerate a realistic sequence.\n\nExample structure:\n\nPhase\nTask\nOwner\nEstimated time\nDependencies\nPriority\n\nPersist the generated roadmap.\n\nAllow converting roadmap items into real tasks.\n\n==================================================\n14. REAL TEAM TASK ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nWhen converting roadmap items into tasks:\n\nassign them to actual project members.\n\nPersist assignments.\n\nTask estimated time must contribute to:\n\nWORK REMAINING\n\n==================================================\n15. REAL SCOPE CUTTER\n==================================================\n\nThis is a core feature.\n\nGemini recommends cuts.\n\nThe USER chooses cuts.\n\nThe APPLICATION calculates the consequences.\n\nDo NOT allow Gemini to directly change the project.\n\nWhen a user cuts a feature:\n\npersist the feature state.\n\nRecalculate:\n\nremaining work\ncapacity gap\nproject health\nrisk\nscope score\n\nThe dashboard must immediately reflect the change.\n\n==================================================\n16. REAL RISK DETECTION\n==================================================\n\nRisk detection must use actual project data.\n\nAnalyze:\n\ndeadline\nremaining work\ntask completion\nunfinished critical tasks\nfeature count\nteam capacity\nblocked tasks\n\nProduce:\n\nrisk level\nrisk reasons\nrecommended action\n\nUse deterministic calculations for numerical risk.\n\nUse Gemini for explanation and recommendations.\n\n==================================================\n17. REAL AI RESOURCE MANAGER\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT pretend we have access to third-party credit balances unless an official API provides them.\n\nDo NOT display fake:\n\nGemini 78%\nClaude 84%\nBase44 41%\n\nInstead create a REAL resource manager where the user can add:\n\nTool\nResource type\nBudget/limit\nCurrent usage\nReset date\nNotes\n\nCalculate remaining budget from user-entered data.\n\nIf an official API integration exists and is configured, use it.\n\nOtherwise clearly label the values:\n\nUSER ENTERED\n\nNever present invented balances as real.\n\n==================================================\n18. REAL AI TOOL RECOMMENDER\n==================================================\n\nImplement:\n\nRECOMMEND A TOOL\n\nInput:\n\nTask\nTime available\nTeam skills\nExisting stack\nBudget/resource constraints\n\nUse Gemini to recommend the most appropriate tool or existing stack.\n\nReturn:\n\nRecommended tool\nWhy\nSetup cost\nEstimated time saved\nAlternative\n\nThe recommendation must consider the user\'s actual project.\n\n==================================================\n19. REAL PROJECT HEALTH DASHBOARD\n==================================================\n\nEvery dashboard metric must come from actual project state.\n\nNo hardcoded metrics.\n\nDisplay:\n\nTime remaining\nWork remaining\nCapacity gap\nTask completion\nScope\nProject health\nRisk\nMVP progress\n\nEvery metric must update when the underlying data changes.\n\n==================================================\n20. REAL JUDGE SIMULATOR\n==================================================\n\nUse the actual project.\n\nEvaluate:\n\nInnovation \342\200\224 25%\nProblem Fit \342\200\224 20%\nUsability \342\200\224 20%\nExecution \342\200\224 15%\nImpact \342\200\224 10%\nFeasibility \342\200\224 10%\n\nGenerate through Gemini:\n\nOverall score\nStrengths\nWeaknesses\nWhy you might lose\nTop risks\nFixes\n\nPersist the latest evaluation.\n\nDo not use static scores.\n\n==================================================\n21. REAL PITCH COACH\n==================================================\n\nUse the actual project.\n\nGenerate:\n\nProblem\nWhy it matters\nSolution\nHow it works\nDemo moment\nImpact\nWhy now\n\nGenerate a real 60\342\200\22390 second pitch.\n\nAllow:\n\nRegenerate\nEdit\nCopy\n\nPersist the user\'s final pitch.\n\n==================================================\n22. REAL DEMO FLOW GENERATOR\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nGENERATE DEMO FLOW\n\nGemini should use the actual:\n\nMVP\nfeatures\nproject\nuser journey\njudge criteria\n\nGenerate:\n\nOpening\nProblem\nSolution\nDemo steps\nWow moment\nTechnical explanation\nImpact\nClosing\n\nEstimate:\n\nDemo duration\n\nAllow the user to edit and save the final demo flow.\n\n==================================================\n23. REAL LAUNCH CHECKLIST\n==================================================\n\nCreate launch checklist items based on the actual project.\n\nExamples:\n\nMVP complete\nCritical bugs fixed\nDemo tested\nPitch complete\nREADME complete\nScreenshots\nDemo video\nSubmission\nRepository\nDeployment\n\nUsers can:\n\nAdd item\nEdit item\nComplete item\nDelete item\n\nPersist everything.\n\nCalculate:\n\nLAUNCH READINESS %\n\nfrom actual checklist completion.\n\nNever hardcode it.\n\n==================================================\n24. REAL ACTIVITY FEED\n==================================================\n\nActivity must come from actual events.\n\nExamples:\n\nProject created\nFeature added\nTask completed\nFeature cut\nAI evaluation completed\nMVP generated\nJudge evaluation completed\nPitch updated\n\nPersist activity.\n\nDo not use fake timestamps.\n\n==================================================\n25. REAL PROJECT SWITCHER\n==================================================\n\nIf a user has multiple projects:\n\nshow their actual projects.\n\nSelecting a project loads its real data.\n\nNo cross-project contamination.\n\n==================================================\n26. DEMO MODE\n==================================================\n\nKeep Team DOOM as an explicit demo.\n\nAdd:\n\nTRY DEMO\n\nDemo mode can use the existing polished Team DOOM data.\n\nClearly label:\n\nDEMO MODE\n\nNormal user mode must NEVER automatically load demo data.\n\n==================================================\n27. NO FAKE AI FALLBACKS IN PRODUCTION\n==================================================\n\nDevelopment may use mock responses only if explicitly enabled.\n\nProduction must NEVER silently replace Gemini output with fake AI responses.\n\nIf Gemini fails:\n\nshow:\n\nHALFTIME AI is temporarily unavailable.\n\nAllow:\n\nTRY AGAIN\n\nDo not fabricate an AI response.\n\n==================================================\n28. NO FAKE CREDIT DATA\n==================================================\n\nDo not invent third-party API usage.\n\nIf usage cannot be retrieved automatically:\n\nshow:\n\nUSER ENTERED\n\nor:\n\nNOT CONNECTED\n\nNever present fake numbers as real.\n\n==================================================\n29. DATABASE PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nAll important user state must survive:\n\nrefresh\nlogout/login\ndifferent device\nnew browser session\n\nPersist:\n\nprojects\nideas\nproblem statements\nMVPs\nfeatures\ntasks\nteam members\nroadmaps\nactivities\njudge evaluations\npitches\ndemo flows\nlaunch checklist\n\n==================================================\n30. LOADING / ERROR STATES\n==================================================\n\nEvery real operation needs:\n\nloading\nsuccess\nerror\n\nExamples:\n\nGenerating ideas...\nSaving project...\nEvaluating project...\nGenerating roadmap...\nSaving task...\n\nNever leave a button visually active while an operation is pending.\n\nPrevent duplicate submissions.\n\n==================================================\n31. SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nNever expose:\n\nGEMINI_API_KEY\nSupabase service-role key\n\nClient-side code may only use safe public configuration.\n\nImplement Row Level Security.\n\nValidate server-side inputs.\n\nNever trust project IDs supplied by the browser without authorization checks.\n\n==================================================\n32. FINAL AUDIT\n\nSearch the entire codebase for:\n\nmock\ndummy\nfake\nplaceholder\nhardcoded\nsample\ndemo\nTODO\nComing Soon\n\nFor every occurrence:\n\ndetermine whether it is:\n\nA. legitimate demo mode\n\nB. legitimate empty-state example\n\nC. actual fake functionality\n\nRemove or replace C.\n\nDo not remove legitimate demo mode.\n\n==================================================\n33. FEATURE COMPLETENESS TEST\n\nTest every feature from a brand-new account:\n\nCreate Project\n\342\206\223\nAdd Team\n\342\206\223\nDefine Problem\n\342\206\223\nGenerate Ideas\n\342\206\223\nEvaluate Idea\n\342\206\223\nGenerate MVP\n\342\206\223\nGenerate Roadmap\n\342\206\223\nCreate Tasks\n\342\206\223\nAssign Tasks\n\342\206\223\nTrack Countdown\n\342\206\223\nDetect Risk\n\342\206\223\nRecommend Tools\n\342\206\223\nManage Resources\n\342\206\223\nCut Scope\n\342\206\223\nUpdate Health\n\342\206\223\nJudge Project\n\342\206\223\nGenerate Pitch\n\342\206\223\nGenerate Demo Flow\n\342\206\223\nComplete Launch Checklist\n\nEvery step must use the CURRENT user\'s CURRENT project.\n\n==================================================\n34. PRODUCTION RULE\n\nThere must be NO dummy data in the normal production experience.\n\nIf a feature cannot be genuinely implemented:\n\nDO NOT fake it.\n\nInstead show a clear state such as:\n\nNOT CONNECTED\n\nor\n\nCONFIGURATION REQUIRED\n\nor remove the feature from the normal user flow until it is functional.\n\n==================================================\n35. FINAL VERIFICATION\n\nRun:\n\nnpm install\nnpm run build\n\nThen test:\n\n- new user\n- authentication\n- project creation\n- project persistence\n- project isolation\n- Gemini\n- tasks\n- features\n- Scope Cutter\n- countdown\n- risk detection\n- Judge Mode\n- Pitch Coach\n- Demo Flow\n- Launch Checklist\n- mobile\n- logout/login\n- refresh\n\nDo not report a feature as complete unless you actually verify its behavior.\n\nAt the end provide a table:\n\nFEATURE | REAL / PARTIAL / NOT IMPLEMENTED | HOW IT WORKS\n\nDo not claim success based only on source-code inspection.\n\nThe goal is:\n\nNO DUMMIES.\nNO FAKE AI.\nNO HARDCODED USER DATA.\nNO VISUAL-ONLY BUTTONS.\n\nHALFTIME must behave like a real application used by real people."
