    response: "I have resolved the `Invalid supabaseUrl` error by adding strict, defensive initialization logic to the Supabase client wrapper.\n\n### Summary of Fixes:\n- **Strict URL & Key Validation**: Added URI schema and placeholder verification (`isValidHttpUrl` and `isValidAnonKey`) in `src/lib/supabase.ts` to inspect the `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` before instantiating `@supabase/supabase-js`.\n- **Fault-Tolerant Client Factory**: Enclosed client instantiation in a safe helper with fallback guards. If placeholder values, malformed URLs, or unconfigured variables are detected, the app automatically and seamlessly falls back to isolated local storage and unique client sessions without throwing runtime exceptions."
    modified_response: "I have resolved the `Invalid supabaseUrl` error by adding strict, defensive initialization logic to the Supabase client wrapper.\n\n### Summary of Fixes:\n- **Strict URL & Key Validation**: Added URI schema and placeholder verification (`isValidHttpUrl` and `isValidAnonKey`) in `src/lib/supabase.ts` to inspect the `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` before instantiating `@supabase/supabase-js`.\n- **Fault-Tolerant Client Factory**: Enclosed client instantiation in a safe helper with fallback guards. If placeholder values, malformed URLs, or unconfigured variables are detected, the app automatically and seamlessly falls back to isolated local storage and unique client sessions without throwing runtime exceptions."
