steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787482628
      nanos: 289926660
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 CRITICAL FIX: NO SILENT LOCAL STORAGE FALLBACK\n\nThe Supabase initialization error has been resolved, but the current fallback behavior is NOT acceptable for production.\n\nThe application currently falls back to localStorage when Supabase configuration is missing or invalid.\n\nREMOVE THIS BEHAVIOR FROM PRODUCTION.\n\nI explicitly do NOT want a fake/offline/localStorage implementation presented as the real application.\n\n==================================================\nPRODUCTION DATA RULE\n==================================================\n\nIn normal production mode:\n\nSupabase configured\n\342\206\222 use Supabase\n\nSupabase unavailable\n\342\206\222 show a clear configuration/error state\n\nNEVER:\n\nSupabase unavailable\n\342\206\222 silently use localStorage\n\n==================================================\n1. REMOVE SILENT FALLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemove the automatic localStorage fallback from the Supabase client/data layer.\n\nDo not silently switch databases.\n\nDo not silently create an isolated local session.\n\nDo not make the application appear to have persistent multi-user storage when it does not.\n\n==================================================\n2. CONFIGURATION ERROR\n==================================================\n\nIf:\n\nVITE_SUPABASE_URL\n\nor\n\nVITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY\n\nis missing or invalid:\n\nshow a clear configuration error.\n\nExample:\n\n\"HALFTIME storage is not configured.\"\n\nDevelopment details may be shown only in development mode.\n\nDo NOT expose secrets.\n\n==================================================\n3. REAL SUPABASE ONLY\n==================================================\n\nAll normal production project data must use Supabase.\n\nThis includes:\n\nprojects\nteam_members\ntasks\nfeatures\nideas\nproblem statements\nMVP plans\nroadmaps\nactivities\njudge evaluations\npitches\ndemo flows\nlaunch checklist\n\n==================================================\n4. VERIFY THE ACTUAL CONNECTION\n==================================================\n\nDo not merely validate that the URL looks correct.\n\nPerform a real Supabase connectivity test.\n\nVerify:\n\n- Supabase client initializes\n- authentication request works\n- database request works\n- current user can be identified\n- project can be created\n- project can be retrieved\n- project can be updated\n- project can be deleted where appropriate\n\n==================================================\n5. VERIFY PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nTest:\n\nCreate project\n\342\206\223\nSave to Supabase\n\342\206\223\nRefresh browser\n\342\206\223\nLoad project from Supabase\n\nThen:\n\nSign out\n\342\206\223\nSign in again\n\342\206\223\nProject still exists\n\nDo NOT use localStorage as the source of truth.\n\nLocalStorage may only be used for harmless UI preferences such as:\n\n- theme preference\n- sidebar state\n- temporary UI state\n\nIt must NOT store authoritative project data.\n\n==================================================\n6. VERIFY MULTI-USER ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate two test users.\n\nUSER A:\n\nCreate Project A.\n\nUSER B:\n\nCreate Project B.\n\nVerify:\n\nUser A cannot see Project B.\n\nUser B cannot see Project A.\n\nUse Supabase Row Level Security.\n\nDo not rely on frontend filtering for security.\n\n==================================================\n7. VERIFY RLS\n==================================================\n\nCheck that Row Level Security is enabled for all user/project data tables.\n\nPolicies must enforce ownership/access at the database level.\n\nNever trust:\n\nproject_id\nuser_id\n\nprovided by the browser without database authorization.\n\n==================================================\n8. DEMO MODE EXCEPTION\n==================================================\n\nThe only permitted local/demo data is explicit:\n\nTRY DEMO\n\nDemo mode may use the existing Team DOOM demonstration data.\n\nClearly label it:\n\nDEMO MODE\n\nNormal users must never silently enter demo mode.\n\n==================================================\n9. NO FAKE SUCCESS\n==================================================\n\nIf saving a project fails:\n\nDO NOT display:\n\n\"Project created\"\n\nShow:\n\n\"Unable to save your project. Please try again.\"\n\nIf Gemini fails, do not generate fake AI results.\n\nIf Supabase fails, do not switch to fake persistence.\n\n==================================================\n10. FINAL TEST\n\nTest this exact flow:\n\nNew user\n\342\206\223\nSign up\n\342\206\223\nCreate project\n\342\206\223\nProject saved to Supabase\n\342\206\223\nDashboard loads project\n\342\206\223\nAdd task\n\342\206\223\nRefresh\n\342\206\223\nTask remains\n\342\206\223\nGenerate Gemini recommendation\n\342\206\223\nSave recommendation\n\342\206\223\nSign out\n\342\206\223\nSign in\n\342\206\223\nEverything remains\n\nThen test a second user and verify complete data isolation.\n\n==================================================\n11. FINAL REPORT\n\nReport:\n\nSUPABASE CONNECTION: PASS/FAIL\nAUTHENTICATION: PASS/FAIL\nDATABASE: PASS/FAIL\nRLS: PASS/FAIL\nPROJECT CREATION: PASS/FAIL\nPERSISTENCE: PASS/FAIL\nMULTI-USER ISOLATION: PASS/FAIL\nGEMINI: PASS/FAIL\n\nAlso explicitly confirm:\n\n\"Production does not silently fall back to localStorage.\"\n\nDo not claim production readiness unless these tests actually pass."
    items {
      text: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 CRITICAL FIX: NO SILENT LOCAL STORAGE FALLBACK\n\nThe Supabase initialization error has been resolved, but the current fallback behavior is NOT acceptable for production.\n\nThe application currently falls back to localStorage when Supabase configuration is missing or invalid.\n\nREMOVE THIS BEHAVIOR FROM PRODUCTION.\n\nI explicitly do NOT want a fake/offline/localStorage implementation presented as the real application.\n\n==================================================\nPRODUCTION DATA RULE\n==================================================\n\nIn normal production mode:\n\nSupabase configured\n\342\206\222 use Supabase\n\nSupabase unavailable\n\342\206\222 show a clear configuration/error state\n\nNEVER:\n\nSupabase unavailable\n\342\206\222 silently use localStorage\n\n==================================================\n1. REMOVE SILENT FALLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemove the automatic localStorage fallback from the Supabase client/data layer.\n\nDo not silently switch databases.\n\nDo not silently create an isolated local session.\n\nDo not make the application appear to have persistent multi-user storage when it does not.\n\n==================================================\n2. CONFIGURATION ERROR\n==================================================\n\nIf:\n\nVITE_SUPABASE_URL\n\nor\n\nVITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY\n\nis missing or invalid:\n\nshow a clear configuration error.\n\nExample:\n\n\"HALFTIME storage is not configured.\"\n\nDevelopment details may be shown only in development mode.\n\nDo NOT expose secrets.\n\n==================================================\n3. REAL SUPABASE ONLY\n==================================================\n\nAll normal production project data must use Supabase.\n\nThis includes:\n\nprojects\nteam_members\ntasks\nfeatures\nideas\nproblem statements\nMVP plans\nroadmaps\nactivities\njudge evaluations\npitches\ndemo flows\nlaunch checklist\n\n==================================================\n4. VERIFY THE ACTUAL CONNECTION\n==================================================\n\nDo not merely validate that the URL looks correct.\n\nPerform a real Supabase connectivity test.\n\nVerify:\n\n- Supabase client initializes\n- authentication request works\n- database request works\n- current user can be identified\n- project can be created\n- project can be retrieved\n- project can be updated\n- project can be deleted where appropriate\n\n==================================================\n5. VERIFY PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nTest:\n\nCreate project\n\342\206\223\nSave to Supabase\n\342\206\223\nRefresh browser\n\342\206\223\nLoad project from Supabase\n\nThen:\n\nSign out\n\342\206\223\nSign in again\n\342\206\223\nProject still exists\n\nDo NOT use localStorage as the source of truth.\n\nLocalStorage may only be used for harmless UI preferences such as:\n\n- theme preference\n- sidebar state\n- temporary UI state\n\nIt must NOT store authoritative project data.\n\n==================================================\n6. VERIFY MULTI-USER ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate two test users.\n\nUSER A:\n\nCreate Project A.\n\nUSER B:\n\nCreate Project B.\n\nVerify:\n\nUser A cannot see Project B.\n\nUser B cannot see Project A.\n\nUse Supabase Row Level Security.\n\nDo not rely on frontend filtering for security.\n\n==================================================\n7. VERIFY RLS\n==================================================\n\nCheck that Row Level Security is enabled for all user/project data tables.\n\nPolicies must enforce ownership/access at the database level.\n\nNever trust:\n\nproject_id\nuser_id\n\nprovided by the browser without database authorization.\n\n==================================================\n8. DEMO MODE EXCEPTION\n==================================================\n\nThe only permitted local/demo data is explicit:\n\nTRY DEM