  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Production Data**\n\nI\'ve been examining the user\'s requirements for production data handling. The core seems to revolve around a clear, decisive approach: prioritize Supabase when available, but immediately display a configuration or error state if it\'s unavailable. Importantly, there\'s a strong directive against any silent failures. I\'m focusing on the logic needed to implement this conditional behaviour.\n\n\n**Refining Supabase Integration**\n\nI\'ve significantly shifted my focus. Silent fallbacks are out; configuration errors are in. I\'m prioritizing rigorous Supabase connection verification, including initialization, authentication, and database interactions with comprehensive testing. Persisting data securely and preventing multi-user data visibility are now main priorities. I\'ve also added specific checks for Row Level Security to ensure that we are using it and that our policies are appropriate. Finally, I\'ve confirmed that the only exception for local data is demo mode.\n\n\n**Implementing Robust Persistence**\n\nMy approach is hardening, prioritizing data integrity. I am now working on the database schema and RLS policies for `projects` and `project_data` tables in Supabase, specifically the SQL migration file. The goal is complete control: I am defining strict RLS rules for user access, preventing silent failures, and implementing a demo-mode exception for local data. I\'m focusing on rigorous testing of all save operations, ensuring no fake successes are ever displayed.\n\n\n**Verifying Configuration Validity**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the nitty-gritty of ensuring the Supabase configuration is valid. I\'m focusing on rigorously checking the presence and validity of environment variables `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, immediately flagging any deficiencies. I\'m also implementing a `checkSupabaseConnection()` method to confirm a live connection, including authentication status and a simple query, to ensure that the setup is functional, reporting latency. Strict rules apply, especially that we can not proceed if Supabase is not available unless in demo mode.\n\n\n**Designing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the nuances of error handling, a critical element of this process. The top priority is ensuring that failures are always communicated honestly and directly to the user. I\'m focusing on the implementation of a dedicated \"Storage Configuration Error Screen\" to handle the case where Supabase is not configured or fails to connect. This screen will include detailed instructions, a Supabase migration script, and a demo mode sandbox. I\'m building out the flow for the error screen and also the demo mode. The demo mode will display a banner, clearly indicating the sandbox status, with a button to \"Connect Supabase\" or \"Exit Demo.\" Authentication via Supabase will also need careful consideration, including Sign Up, Sign In, and Sign Out flows.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 304056873
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
