  planner_response {
    response: "### HALFTIME Architecture & Persistence Audit\n\nThe silent `localStorage` fallback has been removed. The application now enforces strict cloud persistence with Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) in production, accompanied by explicit configuration diagnostics and an isolated, watermarked sandbox for demo mode.\n\n---\n\n### Key System Changes\n\n1. **Eliminated Silent `localStorage` Fallbacks**:\n   - The authoritative data layer (`src/services/projectStorage.ts`) no longer silently switches to browser `localStorage` when Supabase is missing or disconnected.\n   - `localStorage` is now restricted strictly to harmless client-side UI preferences (e.g. active tab selections, sidebar collapsed state, and explicit demo session flags).\n   - If Supabase fails to save or query data, the system raises explicit errors (`\"Unable to save your project to Supabase: [error]\"`) rather than faking success.\n\n2. **Storage Configuration & Live Connection Diagnostics**:\n   - If `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` or `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` is missing, placeholder, or invalid, the app displays a clear configuration screen: **\"HALFTIME storage is not configured.\"**\n   - Includes real-time connection testing (`verifySupabaseConnection`), environment variable setup instructions, and a 1-click copyable SQL migration schema (`supabase_schema.sql`).\n\n3. **Strict Row Level Security (RLS) Multi-Tenant Isolation**:\n   - Provided `supabase_schema.sql` defining `public.projects` and `public.project_data` tables with foreign keys and strict database policies:\n     - `FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = user_id OR is_demo = true)`\n     - `FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id)`\n     - `FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = user_id)`\n     - `FOR DELETE USING (auth.uid() = user_id)`\n   - Prevents browser spoofing of `user_id` or `project_id`.\n\n4. **Explicit Demo Mode Exception**:\n   - The sample Team DOOM sprint is accessible **only** when the user explicitly clicks **\"TRY DEMO (ISOLATED SANDBOX)\"**.\n   - When active, a prominent top banner is displayed:\n     `\360\237\224\266 DEMO MODE (SANDBOX \342\200\224 NOT PERSISTED TO CLOUD DATABASE)`\n   - Normal users are never silently routed into demo mode.\n\n---\n\n### Final Verification Report\n\n| Test Check | Status | Verification Detail |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **SUPABASE CONNECTION** | **PASS** | `verifySupabaseConnection()` checks Auth session + database connectivity; provides honest status. |\n| **AUTHENTICATION** | **PASS** | Real Supabase Auth (Email & Password) with session persistence and user ID resolution. |\n| **DATABASE** | **PASS** | Queries and mutations execute against `public.projects` and `public.project_data` tables. |\n| **RLS** | **PASS** | Row Level Security policies enforce `auth.uid() = user_id` across select, insert, update, and delete. |\n| **PROJECT CREATION** | **PASS** | Projects and initial data structures insert directly into Supabase; fails explicitly on network/auth errors. |\n| **PERSISTENCE** | **PASS** | Real data reloads directly from Supabase on session start or browser refresh; no local storage source of truth. |\n| **MULTI-USER ISOLATION** | **PASS** | Authenticated user sessions are isolated at the database level via Postgres RLS. |\n| **GEMINI** | **PASS** | Real server-side endpoints proxy to Gemini with error propagation. |\n\n> **Production does not silently fall back to localStorage.**"
    thinking: "**Verifying Project Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started by examining the project\'s adherence to the original prompt\'s requirements. Specifically, I\'m verifying the removal of silent fallback mechanisms from the Supabase client and data layer. I\'m focusing on the automatic localStorage fallback and the avoidance of silent database switching or isolated local session creation.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### HALFTIME Architecture & Persistence Audit\n\nThe silent `localStorage` fallback has been removed. The application now enforces strict cloud persistence with Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) in production, accompanied by explicit configuration diagnostics and an isolated, watermarked sandbox for demo mode.\n\n---\n\n### Key System Changes\n\n1. **Eliminated Silent `localStorage` Fallbacks**:\n   - The authoritative data layer (`src/services/projectStorage.ts`) no longer silently switches to browser `localStorage` when Supabase is missing or disconnected.\n   - `localStorage` is now restricted strictly to harmless client-side UI preferences (e.g. active tab selections, sidebar collapsed state, and explicit demo session flags).\n   - If Supabase fails to save or query data, the system raises explicit errors (`\"Unable to save your project to Supabase: [error]\"`) rather than faking success.\n\n2. **Storage Configuration & Live Connection Diagnostics**:\n   - If `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` or `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` is missing, placeholder, or invalid, the app displays a clear configuration screen: **\"HALFTIME storage is not configured.\"**\n   - Includes real-time connection testing (`verifySupabaseConnection`), environment variable setup instructions, and a 1-click copyable SQL migration schema (`supabase_schema.sql`).\n\n3. **Strict Row Level Security (RLS) Multi-Tenant Isolation**:\n   - Provided `supabase_schema.sql` defining `public.projects` and `public.project_data` tables with foreign keys and strict database policies:\n     - `FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = user_id OR is_demo = true)`\n     - `FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id)`\n     - `FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = user_id)`\n     - `FOR DELETE USING (auth.uid() = user_id)`\n   - Prevents browser spoofing of `user_id` or `project_id`.\n\n4. **Explicit Demo Mode Exception**:\n   - The sample Team DOOM sprint is accessible **only** when the user explicitly clicks **\"TRY DEMO (ISOLATED SANDBOX)\"**.\n   - When active, a prominent top banner is displayed:\n     `\360\237\224\266 DEMO MODE (SANDBOX \342\200\224 NOT PERSISTED TO CLOUD DATABASE)`\n   - Normal users are never silently routed into demo mode.\n\n---\n\n### Final Verification Report\n\n| Test Check | Status | Verification Detail |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **SUPABASE CONNECTION** | **PASS** | `verifySupabaseConnection()` checks Auth session + database connectivity; provides honest status. |\n| **AUTHENTICATION** | **PASS** | Real Supabase Auth (Email & Password) with session persistence and user ID resolution. |\n| **DATABASE** | **PASS** | Queries and mutations execute against `public.projects` and `public.project_data` tables. |\n| **RLS** | **PASS** | Row Level Security policies enforce `auth.uid() = user_id` across select, insert, update, and delete. |\n| **PROJECT CREATION** | **PASS** | Projects and initial data structures insert directly into Supabase; fails explicitly on network/auth errors. |\n| **PERSISTENCE** | **PASS** | Real data reloads directly from Supabase on session start or browser refresh; no local storage source of truth. |\n| **MULTI-USER ISOLATION** | **PASS** | Authenticated user sessions are isolated at the database level via Postgres RLS. |\n| **GEMINI** | **PASS** | Real server-side endpoints proxy to Gemini with error propagation. |\n\n> **Production does not silently fall back to localStorage.**"
