  planner_response {
    response: "Here is the database and storage audit comparing the application codebase (`src/services/projectStorage.ts`, `src/App.tsx`, and UI components) against the schema defined in `/supabase/schema.sql`.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Which data is currently persisted in Supabase?\n\nWhen a user is authenticated and Supabase is configured, the application currently reads and writes the following data via `src/services/projectStorage.ts`:\n\n* **In `public.projects`:**\n  * Project metadata: `id`, `user_id`, `name`, `hackathon_name`, `description` (problem statement), `deadline`, `team_name`, `team_members` (JSONB array), `team_skills` (JSONB array), `is_demo`, `created_at`, `updated_at`.\n* **In `public.project_data` (JSONB document store):**\n  * **Tasks**: Sprint tasks array (`title`, `owner`, `role`, `priority`, `status`, `estimatedTime`, `estimatedMinutes`, `reason`).\n  * **Features & MVP Plans**: MVP feature items array (`name`, `description`, `estimatedHours`, `priority`: `MUST_BUILD` | `SHOULD_BUILD` | `NICE_TO_HAVE` | `CUT`, `demoCritical`, `category`).\n  * **Scope Items**: Scope cut items array (`name`, `category`, `timeMinutes`, `reason`, `impactScore`, `selectedForCut`, `isCut`).\n  * **Ideas**: Synthesized hackathon concepts array (`title`, `problem`, `targetUser`, `solution`, scores for innovation/feasibility/usability/impact, `verdict`, `tags`).\n  * **Activities**: Sprint timeline events array (`title`, `timestamp`, `type`, `badgeColor`).\n  * **Judge Evaluations**: AI rubric assessment (`overallScore`, `statusLabel`, `criteria`, `whyYouMightLose`, `fixes` with toggle status `applied`, `summaryFeedback`).\n  * **Launch Checklist**: Pre-flight gates array (`label`, `category`, `status`: `COMPLETE` | `NEEDS_ATTENTION` | `NOT_STARTED`, `detail`, `timeToFinish`).\n  * **Resources**: Tracked AI tools & quotas array (`tool`, `provider`, `budgetLimit`, `currentUsage`, `remainingPercent`, `burnRate`).\n  * **Scope Cut Flag**: `scope_cut_applied` (boolean).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Which data is currently only React/local state?\n\nThe following features exist **strictly in component memory** (`useState`) and are lost on page refresh:\n\n1. **Pitches (`pitchData`)**: Generated in `src/components/launch/LaunchView.tsx` (`useState<PitchCoachResult | null>`). The problem/solution/script/takeaway is generated on demand with Gemini but is **not** included in `ProjectFullData` and is **not** sent to Supabase.\n2. **Demo Flows (`demoFlowResult`)**: Generated in `src/components/launch/LaunchView.tsx` (`useState<DemoFlowResult | null>`). The 3-minute demo script steps and fallback contingencies are **not** persisted to Supabase.\n3. **Active Task Timer**: `activeTaskSeconds` and `isTaskActive` in `src/App.tsx`.\n4. **UI Modals & Navigation**: `isReasoningOpen`, `isShipModeOpen`, `isCommandPaletteOpen`, `isProjectSwitcherOpen`, `isAuthModalOpen`, and `toasts` in `src/App.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Which data is stored in localStorage?\n\n`localStorage` is used **only for client-side UI preferences**, never as the authoritative source of truth for project content:\n\n* `halftime_active_project_id`: Stores the string ID of the currently selected project to restore selection after page reload.\n* `halftime_demo_mode_active`: Stores `\'true\'` or `\'false\'` to track if the user clicked the isolated sandbox demo.\n* `halftime_sidebar_collapsed`: Tracks whether the sidebar is collapsed.\n\n*No projects, tasks, features, ideas, judge scores, or checklists are read from or written to localStorage in production mode.*\n\n---\n\n### 4. Which data requires additional Supabase tables or schema additions?\n\nDepending on whether you choose a **Document model** or a **Normalized Relational model**:\n\n* **If using the Document model (`project_data` table):**\n  * `public.project_data` needs two additional JSONB columns:\n    1. `pitch JSONB DEFAULT NULL` (to persist AI pitch decks and spoken scripts).\n    2. `demo_flow JSONB DEFAULT NULL` (to persist 3-minute demo steps and judge checkpoints).\n* **If using a Normalized Relational model (individual rows per entity):**\n  * The current schema in `/supabase/schema.sql` is missing the following 7 normalized tables:\n    1. `ideas` (title, problem, target_user, solution, scores, verdict, tags)\n    2. `scope_items` (name, time_minutes, reason, impact_score, is_cut)\n    3. `judge_evaluations` (overall_score, why_you_might_lose, summary_feedback, criteria, fixes)\n    4. `launch_checklists` (label, category, status, detail, time_to_finish)\n    5. `resources` (tool, provider, budget_limit, current_usage, burn_rate)\n    6. `pitches` (problem, solution, script, duration, takeaway)\n    7. `demo_flows` (steps, timing, checkpoints, contingency_plan)\n\n---\n\n### 5. Is there currently a `project_data` table?\n\n* **In `/supabase/schema.sql` (the file you reviewed):** **NO.** It only defines `projects`, `tasks`, `features`, `team_members`, and `activities`.\n* **In the codebase (`/supabase_schema.sql` at root):** **YES.** A separate root schema file exists that defines `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.project_data (...)`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Does the application actually use `project_data`?\n\n**YES.** All application data persistence is routed directly through `public.project_data`:\n* `src/services/projectStorage.ts` Line 217: `supabase.from(\'project_data\').insert(...)`\n* `src/services/projectStorage.ts` Line 288: `supabase.from(\'project_data\').select(\'*\').eq(\'project_id\', projectId)...`\n* `src/services/projectStorage.ts` Line 377: `supabase.from(\'project_data\').upsert(...)`\n\n---\n\n### 7. Does the current SQL schema (`/supabase/schema.sql`) exactly match the application\'s Supabase queries?\n\n**NO, it does not match.**\n1. `/supabase/schema.sql` creates normalized tables (`tasks`, `features`, `team_members`, `activities`) which `projectStorage.ts` **never queries directly**.\n2. `/supabase/schema.sql` **omits `project_data` entirely**.\n3. If you run `/supabase/schema.sql` in Supabase right now, any project creation or load attempt will fail with:\n   `PostgreSQL 42P01: relation \"public.project_data\" does not exist`.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Are there any columns the application expects that are missing from this SQL?\n\n* **In `public.projects`:**\n  * **ID Type mismatch**: `/supabase/schema.sql` declares `id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4()`. However, `src/services/projectStorage.ts` generates formatted string IDs (e.g. `prj_1724410000000_abc123` or `demo-doom`). A Postgres `UUID` column will throw a type constraint error on inserts unless the column is `TEXT` or standard UUID strings are supplied.\n* **In `public.project_data` (entire table missing from this SQL):**\n  * Missing: `project_id`, `user_id`, `tasks`, `features`, `scope_items`, `ideas`, `activities`, `judge_eval`, `launch_checklist`, `resources`, `scope_cut_applied`, `updated_at`.\n\n---\n\n### 9. Are there any tables the application expects that are missing from this SQL?\n\n**YES:**\n* **`public.project_data`** is missing from `/supabase/schema.sql`.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Matrix\n\n| Entity | Application Data Location | In `/supabase/schema.sql`? | Actually Persisted to Supabase? |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Projects** | `public.projects` table | Yes (UUID mismatch) | **Yes** |\n| **Team Members** | `projects.team_members` (JSONB) | As separate table `team_members` | **Yes** (via `projects` row) |\n| **Tasks** | `project_data.tasks` (JSONB) | As separate table `tasks` | **Yes** (via `project_data`) |\n| **Features & MVP Plans** | `project_data.features` (JSONB) | As separate table `features` | **Yes** (via `project_data`) |\n| **Ideas & Problem Statements**| `project_data.ideas` (JSONB) | **Missing** | **Yes** (via `project_data`) |\n| **Roadmaps** | `project_data.tasks` (JSONB) | As separate table `tasks` | **Yes** (via `project_data`) |\n| **Activities** | `project_data.activities` (JSONB) | As separate table `activities` | **Yes** (via `project_data`) |\n| **Judge Evaluations** | `project_data.judge_eval` (JSONB) | **Missing** | **Yes** (via `project_data`) |\n| **Launch Checklist** | `project_data.launch_checklist` (JSONB)| **Missing** | **Yes** (via `project_data`) |\n| **Pitches** | `LaunchView.tsx` (`useState`) | **Missing** | **No** (Local React state only) |\n| **Demo Flows** | `LaunchView.tsx` (`useState`) | **Missing** | **No** (Local React state only) |"
    thinking: "**Analyzing JudgeMode Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the workings of `JudgeMode`. I see that the `evaluation` prop comes from `App.tsx` and is managed with `onUpdateEvaluation` and `onToggleFix`. These functions, in turn, manipulate `judgeEval` in `App.tsx`, which then calls `saveProjectFullData`, storing `judge_eval` within `project_data` in Supabase.\n\n\n**Examining Persistence Details**\n\nI\'ve meticulously reviewed the Supabase persistence model. I can confirm the `public.projects` table stores project metadata, while `public.project_data` contains project-specific JSONB data. This includes tasks, features, scope items, ideas, activities and, crucially, judge evaluations. I\'m cross-referencing this with all of the original requests to ensure complete coverage.\n\n\n**Identifying Local State**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the React/local state variables. The `pitchData` and `demoFlowResult` are stored locally. Also noted are the timer variables, active UI modals, and toast notifications. I\'m focusing on how these interact with the overall data flow, especially concerning persistence and potential loss of data on refresh.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Local Storage Usage**\n\nI\'ve just finished analyzing the use of `localStorage`. I\'ve confirmed that it stores only non-authoritative UI preferences. I see the specific keys for session restore, demo mode, and sidebar collapse, but importantly, no project data or evaluations. So, project-related changes are handled elsewhere, as expected.\n\n\n\n**Evaluating Database Normalization**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the database schema and normalization. It seems the current schema in `/supabase/schema.sql` doesn\'t fully implement a normalized relational model, as it\'s missing specific tables for elements like `ideas`, `scope_items`, and `judge_evaluations`, and so on. Also, `/supabase/schema.sql` indeed defines a `project_data` table with JSONB fields.\n\n\n**Verifying Schema Consistency**\n\nI\'ve discovered a critical discrepancy. The file `/supabase/schema.sql` doesn\'t define `project_data` at all! Yet, the application, in `src/services/projectStorage.ts`, extensively uses `project_data` to read, write, and update project-related information. I\'m seeing direct queries to `project_data` for all project documents, and that the SQL schema is entirely different. This represents a significant architectural divergence that I will need to understand better.\n\n\n"
