  user_input {
    user_response: "HALFTIME \342\200\224 FIX THE REAL SUPABASE SCHEMA\n\nThe database audit found that the current application uses a DOCUMENT MODEL:\n\npublic.projects\n+\npublic.project_data\n\nThe existing /supabase/schema.sql is outdated and MUST NOT be executed as-is.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT redesign the UI.\nDo NOT rebuild the storage architecture.\nDo NOT convert the document model into multiple normalized tables.\nDo NOT introduce unnecessary migrations.\n\nKeep the existing projectStorage.ts architecture because it already reads/writes project_data.\n\n==================================================\n1. CREATE THE CORRECT PROJECTS TABLE\n==================================================\n\nThe application currently generates project IDs as strings such as:\n\nprj_1724410000000_abc123\ndemo-doom\n\nTherefore:\n\nprojects.id MUST be TEXT, not UUID.\n\nCreate/modify:\n\npublic.projects\n\nwith:\n\nid TEXT PRIMARY KEY\nuser_id UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\nname TEXT NOT NULL\nhackathon_name TEXT NOT NULL\ndescription TEXT DEFAULT \'\'\ndeadline TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL\nteam_name TEXT DEFAULT \'My Team\'\nteam_members JSONB DEFAULT \'[]\'::jsonb\nteam_skills JSONB DEFAULT \'[]\'::jsonb\nis_demo BOOLEAN DEFAULT false\ncreated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\nupdated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\n\n==================================================\n2. CREATE PROJECT_DATA\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\npublic.project_data\n\nThe schema must match EXACTLY what:\n\nsrc/services/projectStorage.ts\n\ncurrently reads and writes.\n\nInclude:\n\nid\nproject_id\nuser_id\ntasks\nfeatures\nscope_items\nideas\nactivities\njudge_eval\nlaunch_checklist\nresources\npitch\ndemo_flow\nscope_cut_applied\nupdated_at\n\nUse JSONB for the document fields.\n\nUse sensible defaults:\n\ntasks JSONB DEFAULT \'[]\'::jsonb\nfeatures JSONB DEFAULT \'[]\'::jsonb\nscope_items JSONB DEFAULT \'[]\'::jsonb\nideas JSONB DEFAULT \'[]\'::jsonb\nactivities JSONB DEFAULT \'[]\'::jsonb\njudge_eval JSONB DEFAULT NULL\nlaunch_checklist JSONB DEFAULT \'[]\'::jsonb\nresources JSONB DEFAULT \'[]\'::jsonb\npitch JSONB DEFAULT NULL\ndemo_flow JSONB DEFAULT NULL\nscope_cut_applied BOOLEAN DEFAULT false\nupdated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\n\nUse a suitable primary key and ensure one project_data document exists per project.\n\n==================================================\n3. PROJECT ID RELATIONSHIP\n==================================================\n\nproject_data.project_id must reference:\n\nprojects.id\n\nSince projects.id is TEXT:\n\nproject_data.project_id must also be TEXT.\n\nUse:\n\nFOREIGN KEY (project_id)\nREFERENCES public.projects(id)\nON DELETE CASCADE\n\n==================================================\n4. RLS\n==================================================\n\nEnable RLS on:\n\nprojects\nproject_data\n\nFor projects:\n\nAuthenticated users can SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE only where:\n\nauth.uid() = user_id\n\nDemo projects may be readable if the existing application requires public/demo access.\n\nDo not allow a user to modify another user\'s project.\n\nFor project_data:\n\nA user can access a project_data record ONLY if:\n\nproject_data.user_id = auth.uid()\n\nAND\n\nthe referenced project belongs to auth.uid()\n\nDo not rely on frontend filtering.\n\nDatabase RLS must enforce ownership.\n\n==================================================\n5. INDEXES\n==================================================\n\nCreate indexes on:\n\nprojects.user_id\nproject_data.project_id\nproject_data.user_id\n\n==================================================\n6. PITCH PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nThe audit found:\n\npitchData\n\ncurrently exists only in LaunchView.tsx state.\n\nUpdate the existing storage layer so that generated pitch data is persisted to:\n\nproject_data.pitch\n\nWhen the user:\n\nGenerate Pitch\n\342\206\223\nEdit Pitch\n\342\206\223\nSave Pitch\n\nthe final pitch must be persisted to Supabase.\n\nAfter browser refresh, the pitch must reload.\n\n==================================================\n7. DEMO FLOW PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nThe audit found:\n\ndemoFlowResult\n\ncurrently exists only in LaunchView.tsx state.\n\nUpdate the storage layer so that:\n\nGenerate Demo Flow\n\342\206\223\nEdit Demo Flow\n\342\206\223\nSave Demo Flow\n\npersists to:\n\nproject_data.demo_flow\n\nAfter browser refresh, the demo flow must reload.\n\n==================================================\n8. REMOVE LOCAL AUTHORITATIVE DATA\n==================================================\n\nProduction project data MUST NOT use localStorage as the source of truth.\n\nlocalStorage may remain ONLY for:\n\nsidebar state\nactive project ID\ndemo mode preference\n\nProject content must come from Supabase.\n\n==================================================\n9. REMOVE OUTDATED SCHEMA CONFLICT\n\nDo not leave two contradictory schemas that developers might accidentally execute.\n\nUpdate or replace:\n\n/supabase/schema.sql\n\nso that it reflects the ACTUAL application architecture.\n\nIt must NOT create unused normalized tables:\n\ntasks\nfeatures\nteam_members\nactivities\n\nunless the application actually uses them.\n\nThe source-of-truth schema must be:\n\nprojects\nproject_data\n\n==================================================\n10. DATABASE MIGRATION SAFETY\n\nDo not destroy existing user data.\n\nUse safe CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS / ALTER TABLE logic where appropriate.\n\nIf an existing table conflicts with the required schema, report the migration required instead of silently dropping user data.\n\n==================================================\n11. VERIFY STORAGE CODE\n\nAfter modifying the schema:\n\nInspect:\n\nsrc/services/projectStorage.ts\n\nand ensure every field it reads/writes exists in project_data.\n\nVerify:\n\ncreateProject()\nloadProject()\nsaveProject()\nupdateProject()\n\ncorrectly persist and reload:\n\nprojects\ntasks\nfeatures\nscope items\nideas\nactivities\njudge evaluation\nlaunch checklist\nresources\npitch\ndemo flow\n\n==================================================\n12. TEST REAL PERSISTENCE\n\nTest this exact flow:\n\nSign in\n\342\206\223\nCreate project\n\342\206\223\nSave project\n\342\206\223\nReload browser\n\342\206\223\nProject remains\n\nThen:\n\nAdd task\n\342\206\223\nRefresh\n\342\206\223\nTask remains\n\nAdd feature\n\342\206\223\nRefresh\n\342\206\223\nFeature remains\n\nGenerate idea\n\342\206\223\nSave\n\342\206\223\nRefresh\n\342\206\223\nIdea remains\n\nGenerate pitch\n\342\206\223\nSave\n\342\206\223\nRefresh\n\342\206\223\nPitch remains\n\nGenerate demo flow\n\342\206\223\nSave\n\342\206\223\nRefresh\n\342\206\223\nDemo flow remains\n\n==================================================\n13. MULTI-USER SECURITY TEST\n\nCreate:\n\nUSER A\nProject A\n\nUSER B\nProject B\n\nVerify:\n\nUser A cannot read Project B.\n\nUser B cannot read Project A.\n\nAttempt direct access by changing project_id.\n\nIt must be rejected by RLS.\n\n==================================================\n14. GENERATE THE FINAL SQL\n\nAfter auditing and aligning the application code, generate ONE authoritative SQL migration/schema file:\n\n/supabase/schema.sql\n\nThis file must exactly match the production code.\n\nDo not ask me to manually guess missing columns.\n\n==================================================\n15. DO NOT EXECUTE THE SQL YOURSELF\n\nDo NOT modify the Supabase cloud database automatically.\n\nGenerate the correct SQL and tell me:\n\n\"Run this SQL in Supabase SQL Editor.\"\n\nI will execute it manually.\n\n==================================================\n16. FINAL REPORT\n\nReturn:\n\nDATABASE MODEL:\nDOCUMENT MODEL\n\nTABLES:\nprojects\nproject_data\n\nPERSISTED:\ntasks\nfeatures\nscope items\nideas\nactivities\njudge evaluations\nlaunch checklist\nresources\npitches\ndemo flows\n\nAUTH:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nRLS:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nPROJECT ID COMPATIBILITY:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nREFRESH PERSISTENCE:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nMULTI-USER ISOLATION:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nThen provide the complete final SQL schema.\n\nDo NOT claim production readiness unless the code and schema actually match."
