    thinking: "**Checking Auth Setup**\n\nI\'m currently verifying the implementation of `onAuthStateChange` within `App.tsx`. The goal is to ensure the application automatically handles authentication state changes, specifically when users click confirmation links. I am going to add a listener to automatically detect those events.\n\n\n**Analyzing Confirmation Flow**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously analyzing the email confirmation process, considering the various scenarios and states: signup success, sign-in errors, resending confirmations, and confirmation redirects. I want to build robust logic to handle both successful and failed sign-in attempts when the user is not confirmed. My focus is on providing clear user feedback, graceful error messages, and managing the authentication state appropriately. I also am looking at preventing duplicate accounts.\n\n\n**Reviewing Sign-up Flow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the complete password sign-up process, detailing each step: signup, email verification, and sign-in.  I\'m also working on a helper function for opening the user\'s email provider based on their email domain to aid with confirmation. Moreover, I am inspecting `AuthModal` to design a clear, multi-state authentication interface. I am assessing `AuthModal` states and properties.\n\n\n**Mapping Auth Errors**\n\nI\'m developing a utility function, `formatAuthError`, to translate Supabase Auth error codes into user-friendly messages. I\'m building logic to catch specific error conditions, such as unconfirmed emails, invalid credentials, rate limits, and existing accounts, providing specific user-friendly messages for each. I\'m also including fallback mechanisms and verifying the `resend` function.\n\n\n"
